{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew","id":1165631,"title":"[2E] Kith Conversion (Homebrew)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-06T11:18:41-08:00","id":1165631,"title":"[2E] Kith Conversion (Homebrew)","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">This is the first draft of my guide to kith creation. I hope that it will prove useful to someone.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial, serif\"><u><b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">White Oak Dragon\u2019s Unofficial Guide to Kith Creation</span></b></u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><b>Disclaimer:</b> While I have contributed to a couple Onyx Path projects in the past and thus technically count as an Onyx Path writer, as of the writing of this guide, none of them have been for </span><b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Changeling: The Lost.</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"> The following guide is not canon or official in any capacity. It is my own interpretation and expansion of the kith creation guidelines given in the Second Edition core rulebook. I offer it in the hopes that it will ease the burden of those who feel uncomfortable trying to create or translate their own kiths for the first time.<br /> </span></span></span><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial, serif\"><u><b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">1. </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Purpose</span></b></u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">The first step in creating a new kith is to know what </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">you want. If an existing kith already works for your character concept, you\u2019re golden. If not, and that\u2019s likely the case if you\u2019re reading the guide, you\u2019ll need to decide whether you wish to update a kith from a previous version or create an entirely new one.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><b>Updated Kiths: </b></span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">The advantage to updating an existing kith is that</span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"> much of that </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">much of the</span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"> thought </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">of the kith\u2019s theme</span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"> has already been done previously. Kiths from the first edition of the game are available <a href=\"http://wodcodex.com/wiki/Kiths\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, and ones from the version that David Hill had been working on (as well as the rest of those playtest materials) can be found <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B9HTbTc08O4ISWpIbnU4dmlGY2c/view\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. The homebrewed kiths from the Underhill version can be found in Deionscribe's thread <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e\">here</a>.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial, serif\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Original Kiths: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">The advantage to creating a new kith is that you are not limited to the concepts that have previously been produced, allowing you to explore new ground that hasn\u2019t been touched on previously. It </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">might be a bit more work, but </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">the possibilities are limited only to your own imagination</span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">I think the most important rule when coming up with </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">updating a kith or creating</span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"> a new kith </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">is this: </span><b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Theme is King. </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">This is something that the Storyteller and player must work on together. The player of the character should be able to </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">roughly state</span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"> what it is that they\u2019re hoping to use as the concept of their character. Here are a couple examples:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial, serif\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">A favorite kith: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">\u201cI enjoyed playing a character that had been a hunting hawk in Arcadia back in first edition. Can we update the Windwing kith so that I can play a similar one?\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial, serif\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">A desired role: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">\u201cI want my character to be the greatest doctor that has ever lived, </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">but also play upon the fear people have of medical professionals</span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">. Can I do something like that?\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial, serif\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">A beloved tale: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">\u201cMy favorite story is \u2018The Gingerbread Man\u2019, so I\u2019d love to play with the runaway food archetype. </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Is that possible</span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">?\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">The answer to all of the above is \u201cYes, with a little work.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial, serif\"><u><b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">2. Benefits</span></b></u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Once the group of players have worked out what they\u2019re hoping to play, it is time to dive into the mechanical effects of the kith. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial, serif\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Kith Variants: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">This is by far the easiest way to generate a new kith if you\u2019re hoping to diversify the available kiths with minimal time and effort. To create a kith variant, consider existing kiths, then re-skin them to match the new type and alter the Blessing accordingly. For example, a Minstrel kith could be created by altering the Nightsinger to require a specific instrument, or the Artist </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">kith</span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"> might be made into a Scientist </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">by substituting Science for Crafts </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">in the Blessing</span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">. Not all Skills are equal, though, and allowing a Weaponry specialist to create weapons and gain an exceptional success on all rolls using a Weaponry Specialty would probably be a little overpowered. </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">When creating kith variants, I recommend using equivalent Skills and conditions to the original kith. As a rule of thumb, substituting Mental Skills for Mental Skills would likely be appropriate.</span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"> When attempting to balance the kith mechanically, consider the needs of your game, and set limits accordingly. </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">The players should be challenged, but still have their chance to shine.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial, serif\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">S</span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">kill Benefits: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">If re-skinning an existing kith won\u2019t work for your concept, the next step in updating or creating a new kith is to decide where the kith will excel. </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Consider the character concepts when making this decision. It could also be useful to consider how it plays into the trickery benefit that will be determined next. Here are some examples: </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">The player of the Windwing wanted to be a hunting hawk. Hunting is a task that fits into the Survival Skill, so we\u2019ll go with that as our base. As the character is going to be a bird, it makes sense that they would be intended to do so from the air. We will add in foraging and navigation as potential circumstances for the Blessing to apply, making the Windwings skilled at seeking and finding things from the air in general. This will add some variety to the tasks that Windwings could have performed in Arcadia.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">The player of the doctor wanted to be both a great doctor and terrifying to his patients. </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">We\u2019ll update the Chirurgeon kith for this purpose. Medicine is the obvious choice for the base Skill. Surgical procedures seem to be a good way to go, here, as those are often effective ways to save a life while being more invasive to the patient.</span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">The player wishes to futher add a requirement to use fae tools and materials, encouraging bizarre limb and organ replacements or the use of strange and unnatural implements. This drives home the disturbing aspect of the kith.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">For the player interested in the runaway food archetype, we\u2019ll need to create a new kith. We\u2019ll call this kith a Honeysoul. </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">The Skill for this one is difficult to decide. To live up to the archetype, the runaway food should be desirable to eat but difficult to catch. We could go with Persuasion to reflect an ability to entice others, but the player decides that they\u2019d rather the desirability come from the trickery aspect of the Blessing. That means that we\u2019ll focus on the difficulty to catch the character for the Skill, and use Athletics as our base. The Honeysoul will gain their benefit to Athletics rolls when fleeing pursuers, to reflect the chase theme present in such stories.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial, serif\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Trickery Benefits: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">The </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">t</span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">rickery benefit is </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">the meatier part of the Blessing, and the one that\u2019s hardest to balance. We must once again consider the theme of the kith during this portion, but we must also consider what types of abilities might be available through Contracts or Merits. Ideally, the trickery benefit should not make any Contract pointless to purchase, nor should the Contract make the trickery benefit useless. I recommend considering angles on theme that aren\u2019t already covered in order to find a niche that isn\u2019t fully covered. The default assumption is that a trickery benefit will have a Glamour expenditure and a dice roll associated with it that results in a special effect. If this roll affects other characters, it should probably be contested as well. We are not limited to only this format, however, </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">and some blessings simply won\u2019t fit it</span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">. Here\u2019s some example benefits:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">The Windwing should be able to fly. We\u2019ll also use the default assumption for this one, </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">and require a Glamour expenditure and a dice roll for it. For the dice pool, we\u2019ll need to decide which Attribute + Skill combination makes the most sense. Since flying is a physical action, we\u2019ll assume that we need a Physical Attribute and a Physical Skill. Athletics is the obvious choice for Skill, as that\u2019s where running and swimming would also fit. For the Attribute, we decide upon Stamina, as we find it sensible for Stamina to help determine the duration of flight. </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">The player suggests that one minute per success might be a good duration for the flight, and I agree. I further suggest that it might be easier to fly for longer in the Hedge, and increase the duration to five minutes per success there. We\u2019ll try these numbers out in play and see how they work. We can always adjust them later if we find that they are too short or too long for our needs. I also note that the character must rest between flights, but will at least land safely when the need arises. </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">We now must also consider similar abilities, however. </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">The Talon and Wing Contract also allows the character to fly. We decide that the Blessing will double the character\u2019s Speed while flying, and also allow the character to use their Defense against Firearms. As the Contract </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">has other benefits available as well, this seems like both Contract and Blessing would give a benefit to the character. In my games, I\u2019d even allow the Speed to stack if both were activated.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">For our Chirurgeon, we know that we\u2019ll need to tie the Blessing to the character\u2019s skill as a doctor. We initially consider allowing the character the ability to heal with a touch, but that ability is similar to the Blessing of the Playmate kith as well as several Contracts. On top of that, healing hands doesn\u2019t fit the flavor we\u2019re looking for, either. We decide that a Glamour expenditure will boost the Chirurgeon\u2019s Medicine rolls for the scene, while also reducing the time required to perform medical procedures. This maintains the theme very effectively, and we can adjust the time intervals required according to our needs. For now, we settle on emergency medical treatment requiring one-turn intervals and surgery or long-term medical treatment requiring ten-minute intervals. By allowing a patient to benefit from this effect once per scene instead of once per day, it also means that careful attention from a Chirurgeon can greatly speed the healing process. Of course, healing Contracts could potentially make this less useful, so we\u2019ll need to think of an angle that hasn\u2019t been covered yet. In some stories, such as the myth of the God Asclepius, there are surgeons so skilled that they can treat even the dead. </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">We decide that this is the kind of surgeon the character should be, and make it so that the character can treat the recently dead to bring them back to life. We know we\u2019ll need to set a time limit on this, and we settle on ten minutes as a good compromise between being able to do it successfully and maintaining a sense of urgency about doing so. We can always adjust the time frame later if we feel the need.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">The Honeysoul is a tricky one. We know we want the character to fear being devoured, which means we need to make it desirable for people to do so. We contemplate allowing it to heal people who eat it, but that would basically be the Playmate\u2019s Blessing with physical damage replacing Clarity damage as the consequence. On top of that, healing Contracts could make that a far less tempting option. So instead, we decide that the delicious flesh of a Honeysoul will convert easily into Glamour or Willpower </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">for those who devour it. For each lethal or aggravated wound inflicted upon a Honeysoul by eating them, the consumer can regain one point of Glamour or Willpower. Doing so also inflicts mild Clarity damage on the Honeysoul equal to the number of wounds inflicted if the flesh is offered willingly, or severe Clarity damage if the flesh is taken by force. The player feels that this nicely covers what they\u2019re hoping for from the kith, but I think that since the poor thing is going to be eaten, the Honeysoul deserves a little something extra to help mitigate the suffering. I decide that Honeysouls will be immune to bleeding out, and that they will recover from injuries at twice the normal rate.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial, serif\"><u><b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">3. </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Availability</span></b></u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">The next decision to make when creating the kith is how common you wish for it to be. Ultimately, this really depends on the needs of your story, and thus, it will vary by group and even by game. Any given kith can be as rare or as common as your story requires. Some consideration to how this will affect character interactions is necessary here. If the player\u2019s character is the only Chirurgeon in the city, the character\u2019s gifts will be in much higher demand than they would be if several called the city home. </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">A rare or unique kith might be in higher demand by the Gentry, as well, leading to more frequent attempts to acquire the character. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial, serif\"><u><b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">4. Origins</span></b></u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">When considering </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">the origins of a kith, the first step is to find its core. What is the aspect of this person that makes them resonate with the kith\u2019s theme? Whether the changeling was molded deliberately by their Keeper or became what they were through will or circumstance, this link is important. </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Here are some examples:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">For the Windwing, </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">I suggest that we could </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">have</span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"> the Gentry select those that are experiencing unbridled success, </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">symbolically calling to mind the sensation of soaring</span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">. </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">The player agrees that this could work, but it isn\u2019t what they\u2019re looking for. They suggest that instead it should be a yearning for freedom at the heart of a future Windwing. The idea would be that these individuals would be ones with wasted potential, trapped in circumstances beyond their control. The Gentry giving them the gift of the sky would initially seem to free them from their burdens, until the day they realize that they\u2019ve traded one cage for another. </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">We both like that imagery, so we decide to go with that. A frustrated dreamer, an overwhelmed parent, or a child overburdened with familial expectations </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">might all take to Arcadian skies.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">The easy choice for the Chirurgeon would be to focus on medical professionals, as these would already have skill in the necessary area. We feel that this is a bit too simple, though, and that we\u2019d like to focus on a more symbolic connection. </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">Since doctors intend to make people who are injured or ill feel better, we decide that it is a desire to improve or repair that draws the attention of Gentry looking for a future Chirurgeon. To this, we also add an eye for detail to reflect the high degree of skill that a Chirurgeon would need to develop. With these in place, we can see that a skillful surgeon could still become a Chirurgeon, but one </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">could also be made from a technician or a therapist, provided that they were </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">all </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">dedicated enough </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">to their charges</span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">For Honeysouls, </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">t</span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">he player immediately begins to think of comfort food, and so we decide that it will be those that elicit feelings of comfort and security that make ideal candidates.</span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"> A kindly grand</span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">parent</span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">, </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">a charismatic hotel employee, </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">or a fiercely protective </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">confidante</span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"> could all be potential Honeysouls. </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">While some Honeysouls might be specially prepared by one of the Gentry or its servants to be a delicacy, others might be simple chefs to their Keepers until they infuse themselves with the juices and odors of a thousand decadent meals.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial, serif\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><br /> <br /> <b><u>Updated Kiths</u></b></span></span></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Chirurgeon<br /> <i>How do you feel, sir? No, don\u2019t get up yet. That\u2019s a briarwolf heart beating within your chest now. You might want to increase your red meat intake during your recovery. </i><br /> When recounting their transformations, many changelings speak fearfully of eerie surgeons performing bizarre experiments upon them. These unfortunate souls watched helplessly as bits of hobgoblin and stranger materials were spliced into their bodies, twisting them into horrific new forms. Even death provided no escape, as the Chirurgeons calmly replaced damaged organs and pulled the poor changeling back to suffer once more.<br /> While medical professionals are often favored, it is a precise eye for detail and a desire to bring improvement that the Gentry seek in future Chirurgeons. A dedicated therapist or passionate mechanical engineer make better Chirurgeons than a gifted surgeon who only cares about the paycheck. Many Chirurgeons were partially responsible for their own transformations, forced to reattach their own severed limbs or quickly replace their vital organs as a test of their skill. Many who survived such trials were forced to assist in the creation of other changelings. Others functioned as field surgeons in brutal territorial battles between the Gentry, aiding the wounded and returning the dead to their ranks. Many Chirurgeons flee Arcadia when grateful patients choose to take them along during their own escapes. Others cobble together horrific monstrosities and unleash them, the ensuing rampages acting as distractions while they slip away.<br /> The Courts of the Lost often find Chirurgeons useful, as they ease the healing of wounds that might draw scrutiny from mundane medical professionals. While they cannot reach as far beyond the brink of death on Earth as they could in Arcadia, even the chance to save a beloved ally can make a Chirurgeon indispensable. Despite this, many changelings find Chirurgeons deeply disturbing. The existence of the greatest surgeon in the freehold is often a lonely one.<br /> <i>Darkling: </i>Her features are completely shrouded in shadow, except for the bright glare reflecting off her glasses and the gleaming teeth of her eternal smile. People shudder when she vivisects them with her unseen eyes, but she\u2019s only determining how best to put them back together again.<br /> <i>Ogre: </i>He's more scar than man, his towering frame covered in remembered wounds of bullet and blade. He has witnessed the worst that war has to offer, but leaps into the fray without hesitation. His own body is a small price to pay for a life.<br /> <b>Kith Blessing: </b>When the Chirurgeon uses Medicine to perform surgical procedures involving fae tools or materials, achieving three successes counts as an exceptional success.<br /> <i>Three Surgeons\u2019 Gift: </i>By spending a point of Glamour, a Chirurgeon adds Wyrd to Medicine rolls for the scene and reduces the time required for medical treatment to one-turn intervals for emergency medical treatment and ten-minute intervals for surgery or long-term medical care. The Chirurgeon may downgrade one wound each scene in this manner. Additionally, by spending a point of Willpower, a Chirurgeon may use this blessing to pull a patient from beyond the brink of death. Provided that the victim is reached within ten minutes of suffering a fatal wound, and said wound was not inflicted by cold iron or another bane, the Chirurgeon may attempt to tend the patient as though providing long-term care. Successfully downgrading the wound pulls the patient back into the world of the living, but failure on any roll during the process puts them forever beyond the Chirurgeon\u2019s reach.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> We have a list of 1E kiths that people can use as a reference and link their own updated versions to <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1iBdDevwjjyQvxvc8l2u-e_k-dijNIoCePIMYvRGE_1A/edit\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, thanks to wyrdhamster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","user":"White Oak Dragon","date":".  Added the first draft of my guide to kith creation. 12-13-2017, 10:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T19:39:00-08:00","id":1165743,"title":"","content":"Interesting idea; I'm not sure I'd limit the Kith Blessing to just being with fae tools or materials though, since surgical procedures are in and of themselves not a commonplace occurrence. I'm looking between it and the Artist's blessing of simply using a Crafts specialty, or the Leechfinger's examining a potential target's health. Heck, you may even get away with the Changeling simply using a Medicine specialty that pertains to surgery or treating others.<br /> <br /> I wonder if we should turn this thread into the newest incarnation of the Second Edition Kiths thread. While that thread had many good ideas behind it, it was designed for the David Hill version and is rather extensively filled with Kiths that would require a lot of reworking for the current version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 12-06-2017, 10:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T20:43:05-08:00","id":1165759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1165743#post1165743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if we should turn this thread into the newest incarnation of the Second Edition Kiths thread. While that thread had many good ideas behind it, it was designed for the David Hill version and is rather extensively filled with Kiths that would require a lot of reworking for the current version.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Still fiddling with my 'witchtooth' write up (Trickery is tricky), but I will post it here.<br /> <br /> On Chirurgeon: I would limit the exceptional success to &quot;Medicine rolls made for surgery or with fae tools.&quot; Meaning it applies in both circumstances. All of the flavour, less of the too broadness.I would also suggest that Three Surgeons Gift have a limitation. Perhaps only one of the benefits may be used on a patient per scene? You can bring someone back from the brink of death, but you need to take the regular intervals for emergency care after. you revive them, (still able to help others with you Wyrd boosted, reduced time healing techniques though). Otherwise....it is a little strong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T22:09:14-08:00","id":1165771,"title":"","content":"Here's my Airtouched kith; a bit different from what we've seen before, but I rather like the idea. I'm not entirely sure the special ability is quite right though; may take some fine-tuning.<br /> <br /> <b>Airtouched</b><br /> <br /> <i>You may think walking on sunshine doesn't get old, but trust me, you start to miss the earth after a while.</i><br /> <br /> Not all Changelings were made into figureheads or animals that roamed about. Some Keepers preferred having living snowflakes that would dance as they fell, or dust motes that would hold their place for that perfect, sunset moment. Some wanted living balloons, or perhaps something to kick they wouldn't need to pick up again in a ghoulish sport they created. A few have simply wanted grand but weightless feathers to decorate a particular hat. Their bones are hollowed and filled with air, if not their whole bodies, they are coated in dust that they then become or bits of their weight are picked off without reducing their waistline.<br /> <br /> Even if their transformation translates to simply hitting the ground later and softer, many Changeling have made an escape out of it. Decorations thrown out windows have allowed themselves to keep flying, while others have ridden storms their Keepers made upon a disappointment. Some have even simply snuck out as their feet make the barest of <i>tap</i>s upon landing. Some have even found pits in the ground, following them down at a steady gait, and finding a hole out hidden by the bodies of others who were not so gifted with landing.<br /> <br /> For whatever or however they were made, the Airtouched have a unique relationship with gravity, allowing them to bend the rules. On their own, they cannot defy it - what goes up much come down, as they say - but they are allowed to slip its grip for a small moment and be taken in by a good wind. A good few have Some Airtouched have even experimented with man-made equipment to allow themselves more casual flight, but it isn't easy; gliders, windsuits and even kites are designed to work with a human's weight involved. Still, the dream is there, and few can deny that mimicking the ability to run on wind is fun.<br /> <br /> <i>Darkling:</i> Shadows don't so much cling to her as flow, only to solidify with every downward movement she makes. Be it on a step that isn't there, during a small hop or even simply bringing her hand down, a dark surface forms under her that supports her. She is the queen of shadows, and is never without the air of confidence that defines her.<br /> <br /> <i>Ogre:</i> Wind curls around his legs and thunder cracks instead of static. His skin billows with the clouds of a storm, his chest strong with muscle and a wind waiting to be unleashed. His enemies know to look up, for they know they'd never hear him step down behind them. His eyes crackle with unbidden anger, but his boyfriend brings out the sun in them.<br /> <br /> <b>Kith Blessing:</b> When using Athletics to mitigate damage from falling, the Changeling gets an Exceptional Success on 3 successes instead of 5.<br /> <br /> <i>Zephyr's Grace:</i> The Changeling may reflexively spend a point of Glamour and roll Dexterity + Athletics to call a mist about them. On a success, for the rest of the scene, the Changeling's effective weight is minimized and she falls at a much slower rate, allowing them to jump from greater heights than one would otherwise. Add the Changeling's Wyrd to the number of meters they need to fall before taking any points of damage. The Changeling may also choose to become physically lighter, allowing others (or the wind) to pick her up with considerably less burden and granting a +2 on any rolls that would benefit lighter weight, such as jumping or climbing. On an Exceptional Success the Changeling can reduce her Speed up to her Athletics per turn while in freefall, to a minimum of 1, and may induce some sideways motion in turn.<br /> <br /> Edit: added Jumping bonus<br /> Edit 2: changed Jumping bonus to be more encompassing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 12-07-2017, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T22:20:24-08:00","id":1165775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1165743#post1165743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting idea; I'm not sure I'd limit the Kith Blessing to just being with fae tools or materials though, since surgical procedures are in and of themselves not a commonplace occurrence. I'm looking between it and the Artist's blessing of simply using a Crafts specialty, or the Leechfinger's examining a potential target's health. Heck, you may even get away with the Changeling simply using a Medicine specialty that pertains to surgery or treating others.<br /> <br /> I wonder if we should turn this thread into the newest incarnation of the Second Edition Kiths thread. While that thread had many good ideas behind it, it was designed for the David Hill version and is rather extensively filled with Kiths that would require a lot of reworking for the current version.</div> </div> </div> </div>I figured that it could be, which is why I gave it a more general name. Once I'm able to get my computer to cooperate, I'll edit the first post to include a link to the other one so that it's still easy to find for those using the Underhill version. The idea of trying to do so with my phone fills me with dread. I'll address the Chirurgeon in the next post for the same reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T22:45:21-08:00","id":1165777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1165759#post1165759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed. Still fiddling with my 'witchtooth' write up (Trickery is tricky), but I will post it here.<br /> <br /> On Chirurgeon: I would limit the exceptional success to &amp;quot;Medicine rolls made for surgery or with fae tools.&amp;quot; Meaning it applies in both circumstances. All of the flavour, less of the too broadness.I would also suggest that Three Surgeons Gift have a limitation. Perhaps only one of the benefits may be used on a patient per scene? You can bring someone back from the brink of death, but you need to take the regular intervals for emergency care after. you revive them, (still able to help others with you Wyrd boosted, reduced time healing techniques though). Otherwise....it is a little strong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ultimately, it kind of already works that way. Pulling someone back from the dead would put the patient at a Health track full of aggravated damage except for one lethal, and they'd be unable to downgrade any other wounds until the following scene using this blessing. At that point, emergency medical treatment couldn't do much for them. Or did you mean that they could only use the blessing for a single patient (i.e.: if Patient A is saved from death, Patient B couldn't be)? I apologize if I misunderstood.<br /> <br /> As far as the Skill aptitude goes, I'd originally had it for surgical procedures in general, and I may very well put it back that way. I'd switched it to the fae tools or materials version for the flavor, mainly, as I'd thought that using goblin organ &quot;donors&quot;, Hedge thorn needles, or a scalpel carved from the fang of a briarwolf would be delightfully strange without adding much difficulty. Ultimately, it may be an unnecessary distinction. I'll give it some thought.<br /> <br /> Thank you both for your feedback.<br /> <br /> On the Witchtooth: you could always give them a Tilt or Condition that they can set to strike at a later time under certain circumstances. That's the first thing that came to my mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T22:59:00-08:00","id":1165778,"title":"","content":"I like what you're doing with the Airtouched, Taidragon. I could see adding some sort of benefit to jumping with the blessing as well. It could be something as simple as adding distance or height to their leaps, or something as potent as removing the need to mitigate damage if they leap from a height under their own power. Either way could work well with their light weight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T22:59:40-08:00","id":1165779,"title":"","content":"Here's my own attempt at the Draconic kith with a bit of inspiration I have.<br /> <br /> <b>Draconic</b><br /> <br /> <i>I was First among the equally weak, but here my strengths are many fold.</i><br /> <br /> The cruelest of jokes, some will argue, is being made one of the strongest mortals dwelling in Arcadia, because that strength turns to ashes in the mouth of those who face the True Fae's will. As such, the Draconics were the butt of such jokes, being something of a force of nature given the illusion of free will. Some were beasts who made the lesserfolk tremble, waiting for their hero true to rise up and slay the creature. Others were behemoths of stone, storm, or sea bound to destroy intruders. Others became faceless heroes forced to quest again and again to aid their lady fair. Or perhaps they were the trolls who feared the light of day.<br /> <br /> In the end though, their strength was one of the few things of existence in Arcadia they could trust in, and it won them freedom. The beast struck the weapons from the hero's hand and rampaged their way back to Earth. The behemoths rent the world apart and slipped through the cracks and into the Hedge. The faceless hero romanced a new lady fair who pointed her down a path to freedom. The trolls devoured the moon, so that the sun would forget to rise, walking through the darkness into a new world.<br /> <br /> On Earth, their strength no longer can break the land and sky, yet still it is a thing that those with eyes to see will fear. Their bodies still drips and seethes with barely restrained danger given a all too physical form.<br /> <br /> <b>Kith Blessing:</b> When using Intimidation to enforce their dominance over others, the changeling gets an Exceptional Success on 3 successes instead of 5.<br /> <br /> <i>Dragon's Breath:</i>The changeling may spend a point of Glamour and roll Strength + Athletics to eject a gall of fae matter or energy at a foe as a 1L attack with a range of 10 yards/meters away. They can use this attack up to half their Wyrd (rounded up) times a scene per each expenditure of Glamour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":378,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","user":"haren","date":". 12-08-2017, 06:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T23:17:50-08:00","id":1165781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1165779#post1165779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's my own attempt at the Draconic kith with a bit of inspiration I have.<br /> <br /> <b>Draconic</b><br /> <br /> <i>I was First among the equally weak, but here my strengths are many fold.</i><br /> <br /> The cruelest of jokes, some will argue, is being made one of the strongest mortals dwelling in Arcadia, because that strength turns to ashes in the mouth of those who face the True Fae's will. As such, the Draconics were the butt of such jokes, being something of a force of nature given the illusion of free will. Some were beasts who made the lesserfolk tremble, waiting for their hero true to rise up and slay the creature. Others were behemoths of stone, storm, or sea bound to destroy intruders. Others became faceless heroes forced to quest again and again to aid their lady fair. Or perhaps they were the trolls who feared the light of day.<br /> <br /> In the end though, their strength was one of the few things of existence in Arcadia they could trust in, and it won them freedom. The beast struck the weapons from the hero's hand and rampaged their way back to Earth. The behemoths rent the world apart and slipped through the cracks and into the Hedge. The faceless hero romanced a new lady fair who pointed her down a path to freedom. The trolls devoured the moon, so that the sun would forget to rise, walking through the darkness into a new world.<br /> <br /> On Earth, their strength no longer can break the land and sky, yet still it is a thing that those with eyes to see will fear. Their bodies still drips and seethes with barely restrained danger given a all too physical form.<br /> <br /> <b>Kith Blessing:</b> When using Intimidation to enforce their dominance over others, the changeling gets an Exceptional Success on 3 successes instead of 5.<br /> <br /> <i>Dragon's Breath:</i>The changeling may spend a point of Glamour and roll Strength + Athletics to eject a gall of fae matter or energy at a foe as a 1L attack up to 10 yards/meters away. They can use this attack up to half their Wyrd (rounded up) times a scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this. When their blessing states that they can use the attack 1/2 Wyrd times per scene, is it that they spend one Glamour and get that many attacks, or is it that they spend one Glamour for each attack? If the latter, I could see removing the hard limit on the number of times that they could use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T23:21:39-08:00","id":1165782,"title":"","content":"I was thinking the second, but that's probably my tendency to lowball these things. Considering I agreed with your comment on the Airtouched, I think I'll change the wording so it's clearly the first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T00:58:04-08:00","id":1165788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1165778#post1165778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like what you're doing with the Airtouched, Taidragon. I could see adding some sort of benefit to jumping with the blessing as well. It could be something as simple as adding distance or height to their leaps, or something as potent as removing the need to mitigate damage if they leap from a height under their own power. Either way could work well with their light weight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, I was thinking on that but I wasn't sure how to work it in to jumping. I wouldn't remove them needing to mitigate damage on a jump from their own power, as that could get silly and rules-lawyery. I wonder how jumping actually works here...<br /> <br /> *checks the book*<br /> <br /> Turns out that jumping is a simply Strength + Athletics roll. :-p Still, Seven-League Leap is a thing...hmmm, but then again, this would be a general buff as opposed to the contract's one-turn use. Perhaps a simple +2 die bonus would suffice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T01:02:36-08:00","id":1165789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1165779#post1165779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Dragon's Breath:</i>The changeling may spend a point of Glamour and roll Strength + Athletics to eject a gall of fae matter or energy at a foe as a 1L attack up to 10 yards/meters away. They can use this attack up to half their Wyrd (rounded up) times a scene per each expenditure of Glamour.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an interesting kith blessing, but I'm curious; what form would this &quot;fae matter or energy&quot; take? Is it meant to be a sort of element, like the various Elemental Seeming clauses draw from? Could a Draconic have an attack of fire, electricity, acid or a ball of compressed air?<br /> <br /> Also, ahg, double post, my bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T04:39:39-08:00","id":1165820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the Witchtooth: you could always give them a Tilt or Condition that they can set to strike at a later time under certain circumstances. That's the first thing that came to my mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Found a Condition which is perfect...except for resolution. So between that, tweaking the limited Occult boost, working out the 'spam limit' and formatting, I'll be done soonish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T06:42:51-08:00","id":1165847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1165789#post1165789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is an interesting kith blessing, but I'm curious; what form would this &amp;quot;fae matter or energy&amp;quot; take? Is it meant to be a sort of element, like the various Elemental Seeming clauses draw from? Could a Draconic have an attack of fire, electricity, acid or a ball of compressed air?<br /> <br /> Also, ahg, double post, my bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>My impression was that it was basically a breath weapon that the player could re-skin to whatever they needed for their character, so it could be any of the above.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T06:47:52-08:00","id":1165851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1165788#post1165788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmmm, I was thinking on that but I wasn't sure how to work it in to jumping. I wouldn't remove them needing to mitigate damage on a jump from their own power, as that could get silly and rules-lawyery. I wonder how jumping actually works here...<br /> <br /> *checks the book*<br /> <br /> Turns out that jumping is a simply Strength + Athletics roll. :-p Still, Seven-League Leap is a thing...hmmm, but then again, this would be a general buff as opposed to the contract's one-turn use. Perhaps a simple +2 die bonus would suffice?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I'm misremembering, but didn't jumping also have a limit based on character Size? If so, you could also remove that limit in addition to giving them the +2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T07:18:12-08:00","id":1165862,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it could be any of those, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"309\" data-vbnamecard=\"309\">White Oak Dragon</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5803_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5803\" data-vbnamecard=\"5803\">Taidragon</a>. I could see it being an Elemental Draconic firing a hunk of themself in a blast of fire, ice, or earth. A Beast might throw a spine or spit acid. A Fairest hero maybe throws a strangely roselike weapon that seems to appear in their hand from nowhere (or come from the vines bound to their arms like some sort of obscene tattoo) and break with a single use. Stuff like that. The idea is that the attack is sudden, comes in a form from their mein directly, and is single use per &quot;shot&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":378,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","user":"haren","date":". 12-07-2017, 10:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T13:26:01-08:00","id":1165927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1165851#post1165851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe I'm misremembering, but didn't jumping also have a limit based on character Size? If so, you could also remove that limit in addition to giving them the +2.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as the Chronicles of Darkness book states on page 71, Jumping is simply Strength + Athletics. That said, I'm now wondering if I should make that a +2 to &quot;jumping, climbing or any action that would benefit to lessened weight&quot;...and also changing the name to something like Motesoul, since Airtouched in the classic game granted speed and initiative, whereas the David Hill version granted the not-being-hurt-by-falling aspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T14:49:54-08:00","id":1165951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1165927#post1165927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as the Chronicles of Darkness book states on page 71, Jumping is simply Strength + Athletics. That said, I'm now wondering if I should make that a +2 to &amp;quot;jumping, climbing or any action that would benefit to lessened weight&amp;quot;...and also changing the name to something like Motesoul, since Airtouched in the classic game granted speed and initiative, whereas the David Hill version granted the not-being-hurt-by-falling aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see that. As far as the name change goes, that's really your call. Since all of these are unofficial conversions, you really just need to justify the kith by its theme, rather than by what their blessings were in other versions. I saw no problem with Airtouched as the name for your kith, but Motesoul doesn't have a bad ring to it either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T18:13:36-08:00","id":1165987,"title":"","content":"So I haven't done the full writeup because typing is still hard right now, but this is one my favourite Underhill Kiths. It's a pretty straight conversion, and admittedly it was driven in large part by my desire to have blessing based on Science rolls. <br /> <br /> <b>Grey</b> <br /> <br /> <b>Kith Blessing</b>: When the Grey makes a Science roll relating to cutting edge or hypothetical technologies, achieving three successes counts as an exceptional success. <br /> <br /> <i>Mind Probe</i>: Spend a point of Glamour to activate this blessing for the scene. With a successful Presence + Empathy roll, a Grey may use the Telepathy (***) (<b>Chronicles of Darkness </b>pg 60) on someone she is touching or is looking into the eyes of. Using Telepathy in this way does not require spending Willpower.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T19:49:36-08:00","id":1166006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1165782#post1165782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking the second, but that's probably my tendency to lowball these things. Considering I agreed with your comment on the Airtouched, I think I'll change the wording so it's clearly the first.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you make it 1 glamour per shot, consider instead giving it a damage of wyrd [cap at 5] and remove the line about shot limit. This would be a fair trade for the 1 glamour.<br /> <br /> Alternatively making wyrd 1L shots, is also fair for 1 Glamour. Both are good choices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T03:46:29-08:00","id":1166049,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar600_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"600\" data-vbnamecard=\"600\">HaplessWithDice</a> I already had increased it, but I have changed the range of the shot in that it actually uses the range rules. But as a point, 1L means &quot;You get your successes on an attack roll + 1 Lethal damage.&quot; This is equivalent to a light pistol, just without the taking away of Defense by a firearm. So you know, it's not as good as a gun in that way, but it's still pretty solid. Mostly the reason it still allows Defense is because this is a Wyrd based attack and if feels right that you have a CHANCE to avoid the attack because even the True Fae have holes in their power. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":378,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","user":"haren","date":". 12-08-2017, 07:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T05:25:00-08:00","id":1166061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1166049#post1166049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar600_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"600\" data-vbnamecard=\"600\">HaplessWithDice</a> I already had increased it, but I have changed the range of the shot in that it actually uses the range rules. But as a point, 1L means &quot;You get your successes on an attack roll + 1 Lethal damage.&quot; This is equivalent to a light pistol, just without the taking away of Defense by a firearm. So you know, it's not as good as a gun in that way, but it's still pretty solid. Mostly the reason it still allows Defense is because this is a Wyrd based attack and if feels right that you have a CHANCE to avoid the attack because even the True Fae have holes in their power. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>True it is equivalent to a thrown hatchet. The reason I brought up the scaled up damage is there is another dragon fire breath attack in Chronicles of Darkness although it is a sustained fire breath instead of a singular ball or quick beam of energy. Dragon Fire from Beast. If we look to that one as an example it has a damage of Supernatural Tolerance. It in my book would be safe to bet that a Primordial dragon and a Lost dragon should be about as powerful as each other since both are dragons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T05:35:32-08:00","id":1166063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1166061#post1166061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True it is equivalent to a thrown hatchet. The reason I brought up the scaled up damage is there is another dragon fire breath attack in Chronicles of Darkness although it is a sustained fire breath instead of a singular ball or quick beam of energy. Dragon Fire from Beast. If we look to that one as an example it has a damage of Supernatural Tolerance. It in my book would be safe to bet that a Primordial dragon and a Lost dragon should be about as powerful as each other since both are dragons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to point out that is an Atavism. I'm not saying you're wrong about Dragonfire, but I feel like this is at a good power level for a &quot;free&quot; benefit (and has double the range of Dragonfire). I do appreciate your input, and you did convince me to make one change. Also, Beasts seem to be a bit more physically intimidating by default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T11:12:59-08:00","id":1166132,"title":"","content":"Hey guys. Here's the write up I've been working on for the Weisse Frau Kith (my favorite of the Underhill Kiths). I feel like I'm on the right track, but the second aspect of the kith blessing is what\u2019s been giving me the most trouble. I\u2019m thinking the changeling can either give another character a +1 die bonus to resisting clarity/breaking point rolls, or just give another character that +1 bonus to their next roll, whatever it is I want Weisse Frau\u2019s to be something of a support class, socially speaking, so some guidance there would be aces.<br /> <br /> <u>Weisse Frau </u><br /> <br /> <i>Alright honey, have a seat, I'll tell you exactly how I can help you.</i><br /> <br /> These changelings are created by their keepers for a very specific and to some extent, reviled purpose. To lure individuals into the hedge. For while the gentry can seduce a person through the hedge, or bind them in a net and drag them through, but one thing they can\u2019t do, aren\u2019t capable of doing, is to connect with people, create a genuine bond that can coax people through the thorns. So for that, they groom their weisse frau, changelings that already have a natural aura of friendliness and amiability, and aplify that. Sometimes the weisse frau know the fate they are subjecting their companions to, having been broken by their keepers, or threatened. Other times, they sincerely believe that they\u2019re doing their targets a favor. But eventually, one can\u2019t take it anymore. They learn the truth, or stop being able to stomach the truth they already know. And when they do, they escape, or simply never return, renouncing their past and their keepers. Now they stand protect those around them, the weak and young especially. Perhaps if they protect enough people, it will make up for all those they\u2019ve already damned.<br /> <br /> Darkling: She\u2019s plain, non-threatening, blends into the background. But she\u2019s a comforting presence, and she has a beautiful voice. That\u2019s the only part you can really remember-everything else was so\u2026plain, so generic. But that voice, it lingers in your ears. It soothes you like a drug, made you want to stop and chat and get to know this woman. You don\u2019t care about the thorns scratching you-she says they\u2019re all safe.<br /> <br /> Wizened: She\u2019s like everybody's favorite aunt, or grandmother. She always knows exactly the right words to make you laugh, or to calm you down. Her eyes are big and genuine, as if they\u2019re searching your soul for what makes you smile. Her skin is so soft you just want to use her like a pillow. She seems so small and harmless and sweet, why wouldn\u2019t you follow her through that archway? She would never hurt you-look at her, she couldn\u2019t even if she tried.<br /> <br /> Kith Blessing: When the Weisse Frau makes an empathy or persuasion roll to calm or sooth a target, they earn an exceptional success on three successes instead of five.<br /> <br /> (EDIT: the following came from the brilliant Taidragon)<br /> <br /> <i>Trust In Me:</i> When the Weisse Frau is with someone in emotional turmoil, be it a Breaking Point or receving Clarity damage, she may spend a point of Glamour to fix their attention upon herself and become a fixed point in an unstable malady. She can do this even if she isn't aware of the event itself, so long as she is offering some form of comforting presence itself for the person undergoing the trauma - it is a reflexive action for her. If it is a Changeling undergoing Clarity damage, they reduce their effective Wyrd for Clarity damage by the Weisse Frau's own Wyrd; if this results in effectively 0 Wyrd, the damage is reduced to a Chance die. If it is a mortal undergoing a Breaking Point, she may instead bolster the roll with half her Wyrd (rounded up). She may do this once per character per scene.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7372-lady-gray","user":"Lady Gray","date":". 12-09-2017, 07:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7372-lady-gray","name":"Lady Gray","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7372_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T12:08:42-08:00","id":1166140,"title":"","content":"I'm fond of the resisting Clarity/Breaking Points personally, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7372-lady-gray\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7372_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7372\" data-vbnamecard=\"7372\">Lady Gray</a> . Here's another Kith, done for a Mage game I'm in where one of the characters is married to a Changeling (and due to Time hijinks, we're still not sure HOW). I'm playing a bit with the Kith Blessing, making it a bit broader in what rolls it affects, for limitations based on a Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Flowering</b><br /> <br /> <i>Love is a funny thing, but I'll tell you this: No one has ever loved the way you do, for each love is unique.</i><br /> <br /> The Language of Flowers isn't an archaic thing in Arcadia, and there are those who were living messages in it. Most often living symbols of Love and Hate. As such they are intimately tied to Love, even if the flower they were has nothing to do with Love. Their natures were both flower and animal. Beasts could be Snapdragons or Lily Tigers. A Darkling could represent messages not so much of an emotion but it's lack or something negative, such as a blackened and dead rose. The Fairest was almost a living stand-in for the one sending the message, being a messanger of Love, and a lover themselves. Ogres were hulking figures with pelts of moss and wild thistle, giving messages of Hate and Vengence. An Elemental was more plant than animal, a flowering treant or something similar. The Wizened often had more artificial flowers of wire and metal leaf bound to their hair and flesh. But in all cases, they were messangers for their Keeper. And often suffered the more for it.<br /> <br /> <b>Kith Blessing:</b> When the Flowering rolls Persuasion on someone Swooning (as in the Condition) towards them, they gain an exceptional success on 3 successes rather than 5.<br /> <br /> <i>Love Springs Eternal:</i> The Flowering can spend a Glamour to release a sweet and cloying perfume that reduces the effective (except for Willpower) Composure of a target by net successes on an opposed Presence + Expression + Wyrd vs Composure + Supernatural Resistance up to a minimum of 1 for the rest of the scene. This affects them when within 10 yards/meters of the Flowering. It's hard to keep one's head clear when a Flowering takes action without getting away from them. If the target's Composure would have gone to 0 or lower based on successes, they are considered Swooned towards the Flowering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":378,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","user":"haren","date":". 12-08-2017, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T13:01:49-08:00","id":1166149,"title":"","content":"<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> I like your Grey writeup a good deal; my suggestion for it would be to simply make the Kith Blessing into a roll using a Science specialty, like the Artist kith uses Crafts Specialties. I'm sure there's a better way of granting the Telepathy merit without actually making it the merit itself, but as far as abilities goes it works.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7372-lady-gray\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7372_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7372\" data-vbnamecard=\"7372\">Lady Gray</a> You are definitely on the right path on your writeup. For your Kith Blessing, I'd use Persuasion as the skill in question, since you're persuading them to calm down and not be agitated, though Empathy may work as well. I love the idea of Weisse Frau going from tempters to protectors. It made me think of this ability for them; let me know what you think of it.<br /> <br /> <i>Trust In Me:</i> When the Weisse Frau is with someone in emotional turmoil, be it a Breaking Point or receving Clarity damage, she may spend a point of Glamour to fix their attention upon herself and become a fixed point in an unstable malady. She can do this even if she isn't aware of the event itself, so long as she is offering some form of comforting presence itself for the person undergoing the trauma - it is a reflexive action for her. If it is a Changeling undergoing Clarity damage, they reduce their effective Wyrd for Clarity damage by the Weisse Frau's own Wyrd; if this results in effectively 0 Wyrd, the damage is reduced to a Chance die. If it is a mortal undergoing a Breaking Point, she may instead bolster the roll with half her Wyrd (rounded up). She may do this once per character per scene.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar378_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"378\" data-vbnamecard=\"378\">haren</a> I love the writeup you have for your Flowering, and your Kith Blessing is spot on. As for &quot;Love Springs Eternal&quot;, it's an interesting ability, though I wonder how effective the -1 to Composure would be in the long run without any scaling. Perhaps make it a Presence + Socialize contested roll, but make it so every success lowers the target's effective Composure? Maybe even make it so you can inflict Swooned on someone if their Composure is dropped to effectively 0 around you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T13:08:43-08:00","id":1166150,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5803_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5803\" data-vbnamecard=\"5803\">Taidragon</a> I'm about to play Path of Exile, but I'll consider that while doing it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T13:51:37-08:00","id":1166157,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about this one recently. It's fairly straightforward, but I wanted to update one of my favorite kiths anyway.<br /> <br /> <b>Swimmerskin</b><br /> <br /> <i>The water is lovely today. Care to join me?</i><br /> <br /> For as long as they have preyed upon humanity, the Strangers have had a preoccupation with oceans, lakes, and all manner of watery landscapes shallow and deep. Some ensconce themselves in Titles such as &quot;Dragon Prince of the Eastern Sea&quot; while others just harbor a fascination for all the treasures sunken and swimming that can be found below the waves.<br /> <br /> Mortals who are turned into Swimmskins tend to already be fish-out-of-water types, those who feel like they don't quite belong, or harbor a deep longing for new vistas. A connection to water certainly helps, and plenty of members of this kith were fishers, divers, or marine biologists in their human lives, but above all appears to be the desire for a completely different situation.<br /> <br /> Others are transformed out of pure necessity; it's difficult to attend to the Mermaid Queen's needs if you're just going clutch your throat and then stop moving after a few minutes, after all. A Swimmerskin might be transformed into a shark, have a bitter-tasting ball of kelp stuffed into her mouth, or wake up on a submerged operating table with a curved breathing apparatus sewn into the sides of her neck.<br /> <br /> It's not talked about much, but many times Swimmerskins feel conflicted about their place in the world. Those especially who already felt a connection to water before their Durances might feel that they owe their former Keeper something akin to a debt of gratitude for the &quot;gifts&quot; the True Fae bestowed on them. In times of Loyalist witchhunts, suspicious eyes may fall on those who spend far too long beneath the waves. Regardless, in Freeholds whose territory includes large bodies of water, the a Swimmerskin's presence can be invaluable. On may help finance his court through diving for sunken curios, while another patrols a serpentine river in the Hedge for fluvial threats.<br /> <br /> <i>Beast:</i> This changeling has the skin of an eel, and all the grace to match. When he smiles, his mouth is full of needle-like teeth--all the better for gulping down fresh fish.<br /> <br /> <i>Fairest:</i> She spends her free time sitting at the edge of a lake, her legs tracing currents in the water, combing her luxurious blue-green-blond hair and singing the loveliest song you've ever heard, one full of both wonderment and homesickness. On a closer look, there is a nearly-translucent webbing between her fingers, and a dusting of shiny scales on her cheeks.<br /> <br /> <b>Kith Blessing:</b> When the Swimmerskin makes an Athletics roll while underwater, achieving three successes counts as an exceptional success.<br /> <br /> <i>Ocean's Kiss</i>: A Swimmerskin can breathe unpolluted water just as easily as air. He may extend this ability to another being by spending a point of Glamour and touching their lips. This lasts for a number of minutes equal to the changeling's Wyrd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T16:36:52-08:00","id":1166191,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5803_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5803\" data-vbnamecard=\"5803\">Taidragon</a> That is brilliant! I think that's the perfect blessing for what I was going for. As for the relevant skill, I'm wondering if I can't tie the blessing to both empathy and persuasion, since it's ambiguous and to a degree either could be used. Though I'm leaning towards empathy since the weisse frau's thing is that they connect with and understand people, and they're using that understanding to calm people down, not so much trying to convince them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7372-lady-gray","name":"Lady Gray","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7372_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T16:46:39-08:00","id":1166193,"title":"","content":"I've been running through and trying to mechanically update a number of Kiths from the initial previews (plus one homebrew original). They're missing fluff, but I feel they should work pretty well.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Truefriend</span><br /> <b>Kith Blessing:</b> When the Truefriend uses Empathy to comfort or understand a companion, three successes count as an exceptional success.<br /> <i>True Bond:</i> If she touches someone she truly cares about and spends a point of Glamour, she may roll Presence + Expression to inspire and reinforce them. If she succeeds on the roll, both she and the person she touched gain the Steadfast Condition. Truefriends automatically resist any powers that would force or coerce them to betray a friend who currently benefits from this gift.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Draconic</span><br /> <b>Kith Blessing:</b> When the Draconic uses Intimidation to cow another through a show of force, three successes count as an exceptional success.<br /> <i>Dreadful Form:</i> The thick scales of the Draconic turn one point of Lethal damage taken from every attack into Bashing damage. If she spends a point of Glamour, her unarmed attacks deal Lethal damage for the rest of the scene and her scales may instead turn one point of Aggravated damage into Lethal or ignore one point of Bashing damage altogether.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Razorhand</span><br /> <b>Kith Blessing:</b> When the Razorhand uses Weaponry with the intent to kill a fae creature at night, three successes count as an exceptional success.<br /> <i>Darkblade:</i> The Razorhand has a natural weapon with 1L damage, which causes lethal damage even to creatures which normally take bashing damage from lethal wounds. If she spends a point of Glamour, a Razorhand can also cause her next successful attack with this weapon to automatically inflict one of the following Tilts: Arm Wrack, Blinded, Deafened, or Leg Wrack.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Smith</span><br /> <b>Kith Blessing:</b> When the Smith uses Craft to build or repair objects with a practical function, three successes count as an exceptional success.<br /> <i>Maker's Deftness:</i> By spending a point of Glamour, the Smith can repair, modify, or sabotage any object with inhuman speed. If the repair or alteration would require an extended action, he makes rolls on the extended task once a turn.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Airtouched</span><br /> <b>Kith Blessing:</b> When the Airtouched uses Athletics to jump, three successes count as an exceptional success.<br /> <i>Lighter Than Air:</i> The Airtouched suffers no falling damage except from falls that reach terminal velocity. If she spends a point of Glamour, she can multiply her jumping height and distance by three for a single roll, and slowly glide instead of falling for the same distance.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Windwing</span><br /> <b>Kith Blessing:</b> When the Airtouched uses Athletics to ascend through the air under the open sky, three successes count as an exceptional success.<br /> <i>Wind-Carried:</i> The Windwing may spend a Glamour and roll Stamina + Athletics to fly at twice her Speed for Stamina turns. Regardless of her real weight she may land and perch on anything that might hold the weight of a small child.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Blightbent</span><br /> <b>Kith Blessing: </b>When the Blightbent uses Survival to navigate or forage in a poisonous, radioactive or otherwise blighted environment, three successes count as an exceptional success.<br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Plague-filled:</span></i> The Blightbent reduces the level of any manmade extreme environment and the Toxicity of any drug or poison by 2. If she spends a point of Glamour she may roll Stamina + Wyrd to produce a cloud of caustic smog with a radius in meters equal to her Stamina. The cloud either causes a concealment penalty or deals lethal damage with Toxicity equal to half the successes on this roll, round up. The cloud lasts for a scene without outside intervention.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Broadback</span><br /> <b>Kith Blessing:</b> When the Broadback uses Athletics in a contest of endurance, three successes count as an exceptional success.<br /> <i>Stoic Forbearance:</i> The Broadback suffers no penalties due to fatigue, and she may spend one point of Glamour to add her Wyrd to Doors in Social Manuevering, adding up to +5 doors.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Coyote</span><br /> <b>Kith Blessing:</b> When the Coyote uses Subterfuge to leave a favorable opinion of himself during a first impression, three successes count as an exceptional success.<br /> <i>Face of a Friend: </i>When attempting Social Maneuvering, the Coyote may spend one Glamour to start one impression level higher than she otherwise would.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Antiquarian</span><br /> <b>Kith Blessing:</b> When the Antiquarian uses Academics to evaluate or research ancient lore, books or artifacts, three successes count as an exceptional success.<br /> <i>Keys to Knowledge:</i> While touching an item more than a century old, the Antiquarian may spend one Glamour to reflexively roll Wits + Investigation + Wyrd. This allows her to perceive the most emotionally intense moment tied to the object, letting you ask the Storyteller a yes or no question related to the scene for each success gathered, or gain the Informed condition pertaining to the item.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Render<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Kith Blessing:</b></span></span>When the Render uses Brawl to destroy an object or structure, three successes count as an exceptional success.<br /> <i>Crumbling Touch:</i> If the Render spends a point of Glamour, for the rest of the scene she ignores worn armor in unarmed attacks and durability in damaging objects.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Skitterskull</span><br /> <b>Kith Blessing:</b> When the Skitterskull uses Athletics to climb, three successes count as an exceptional success.<br /> <i>Impossible Counterpoise:</i> The Skitterskull suffers no penalties to Athletics rolls when climbing even the steepest surfaces, and by spending one Glamour, she can triple her Defense when Dodging instead of Doubling.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Venombite</span><br /> <b>Kith Blessing:</b> When the Venombite uses Brawl to grapple with the intent of delivering a venomous bite, three successes count as an exceptional success.<br /> <i>Kiss of Death:</i> The Venombite may spend a point of Glamour to deliver a venomous bite when using a damage move as part of a grapple. She applies the Moderate version of the Poisoned Tilt to the receiving character. Outside of combat the venom deals damage on a turn basis and has Toxicity 4.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Waterborn</span><br /> <b>Kith Blessing:</b> When the Waterborn uses Athletics while submerged in water, three successes count as an exceptional success.<br /> <i>Like a Fish:</i> The Waterborn can breathe freely underwater, and if she spends a point of Glamour then for the rest of the scene she swims at her full Speed and may make Empathy rolls to sense and understand the strongest feelings felt in a body of water or its immediate vicinity. In open water like the ocean she treats an area of five kilometers like a single body of water.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Swimmerskin</span><br /> <b>Kith Blessing:</b> When the Swimmerskin uses Athletics while swimming, three successes count as an exceptional success.<br /> <i>Ocean's Kiss:</i> A swimmerskin can breathe water as easily as air, and may extend this ability to another being by spending a point of Glamour and rolling Wyrd + Stamina while touching their lips. This lasts for a number of minutes equal to Wyrd.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Runnerswift</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Kith Blessing: </span></b>When the Runnerswift uses Athletics to run from a foe or predator, three successes count as an exceptional success.<br /> <i>League-Gallop:</i> The Runnerswift may spend a point of Glamour and reflexively rolls Dexterity + Athletics. For the rest of the scene, she adds two plus the successes to her Speed, and inflicts a penalty on all dice rolls attempting to track or follow her equal to successes, up to -5.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Flamesiren</span><br /> <b>Kith Blessing:</b> When the Flamesiren uses Expression to fascinate or entrance, three successes count as an exceptional success.<br /> <i>Moths to the Flame:</i> Spend a point of Glamour and roll Presence + Expression + Wyrd as an instant action to perform, contested by anyone who witnesses the Flamesiren's enchanting show with Composure + Supernatural Tolerance. She can inflict a single audience member who fails to resist with the Swooning condition. Anyone afflicted with the Swooning condition in this way who touches the Flamesiren treats her as an Extreme Environment with level equal to half her Wyrd round up.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Soldier</span><br /> <b>Kith Blessing:</b> When the Soldier uses Survival in open conflict with an enemy or in a war-torn battlefield, three successes count as an exceptional success.<br /> <i>Master of Arms:</i> A Soldier does not take Initiative penalties from weapons, and she can spend a Glamour after a full night's sleep to exchange any dots of a Fighting Style Merit she possesses for the same number of dots in other Fighting Style merits. Fighting Styles obtained this way can ignore Attribute and Skill requirements.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Lionheart</span><br /> <b>Kith Blessing:</b> When the Lionheart uses Persuasion to inspire another to follow correct or honest conduct, three successes count as an exceptional success.<br /> <i>Binding of Honor:</i> Once per session, the Lionheart may strengthen a Sealing without the need to spend Willpower. If a changeling attempts to refute such a sealing, the Lionheart may spend a point of Glamour and force him to roll a Clash of Wills of his Wyrd + Resolve against her own, in addition to the usual cost of undoing it. However, the Lionheart is unable to refute a single Sealing placed by a person under the effect of Binding of Honor.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Skogsra</span><br /> <b>Kith Blessing:</b> When the Skogsra uses Stealth to conceal herself or stalk in the wilderness, three successes count as an exceptional success.<br /> <i>Fauna Affinity:</i> If the Skogsra spends a point of Glamour, then for the next scene she can communicate with any wild or feral animals and give them simple commands they will obey with a successful Presence + Animal Ken roll, unless the animal is already under supernatural control or the command is obviously suicidal.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Whisperwind</span><br /> <b>Kith Blessing:</b> When the Whisperwind uses Investigation to gather information through hearing or conversation, three successes count as an exceptional success.<br /> <i>Secrets In the Breeze:</i> The Whisperwind can hear with perfect clarity up to a block away for each dot of Wyrd she possesses, to a maximum of five. By spending a point of Glamour, she can make someone else able to hear her whispers clearly at the same distance.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Gravewright</span><br /> <b>Kith Blessing:</b> When the Gravewright uses Occult to learn about ghosts, three successes count as an exceptional success.<br /> <i>Medium:</i> The Gravewright can see and hear nearby ghosts in Twilight, and may spend a point of Glamour to add or remove the Anchor, Open, Controlled or Materialized Condition to or from an object, person or location, so long as the condition's prerequisites are met. Attempting to restore a condition the Gravewright removed in the last week creates a Clash of Wills.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I would say that out of these, it's the Waterborn and the Broadback that I am the least satisfied with, and which are likely to prone to revision, but feedback on any would be appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 12-08-2017, 10:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T18:15:04-08:00","id":1166214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1166149#post1166149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> I like your Grey writeup a good deal; my suggestion for it would be to simply make the Kith Blessing into a roll using a Science specialty, like the Artist kith uses Crafts Specialties. I'm sure there's a better way of granting the Telepathy merit without actually making it the merit itself, but as far as abilities goes it works.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had that exact comment in there for a while, but it didn't quite fit the way I wanted it to. When I think of Greys in terms of technology, I don't think of all around good scientists. I think of cutting edge, bizarre, and improbable devices, so having a general science blessing didn't seem right. I wanted something that made the Grey feel other worldly and familiar. Plus, as a science teacher, I feel like the science speciality blessing should go to a kith that feels more down to earth, so to speaks. <br /> <br /> As for the merit you're absolutely right, but as I said, I based this on a pretty much straight conversion from Underhill. I just adapted the mechanic from there, so since it referenced the Telepathy merit, so did I. But thanks for the feedback! It is appreciated!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T19:13:15-08:00","id":1166224,"title":"","content":"Honestly if we ever get a more detailed Kith builder, &quot;Pick a three dots of supernatural merits and swap in a glamour cost&quot; seems like a half-way decent baseline for a number of archetypes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T20:02:28-08:00","id":1166230,"title":"","content":"Here is one I posted a while ago...This is the final version.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201c</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i>It is the screams of the children I remember most. The smell of cooked human flesh is exactly like that of pork. I remember them, their faces as they burned, as they screamed and begged for mercy. It is something that haunts me every time. How do I deal with it? For starters...I don\u2019t eat pork.</i></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sometimes the gentry just need to quell a rebellion, destroy a neighbor, or incinerate a hobgoblin village. When they need such an engine of destruction they make an Efreet. These power houses are made from those who have strong burning tempers, not always ones that explode fast but that can build up over time into raging infernos. A passionate personality is required as well. These changelings become avatars of carnage, and flame and when set loose upon their targets leave only ash in their wake.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fairest: An exotic muscular figure with reddish skin and small horns, who when exited or angered seems to be aglow from within.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ogre: A beastial figure of claws, rage, horns, and flame. It\u2019s face that of a predator, and yet very expressive almost human.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Blessing</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When using Craft to demolish a building or other inanimate object, an exceptional success is gained on 3 successes instead of the usual 5.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Burning Wrath</i> - By spending a point of glamour the Efreet can turn their burning wrath into a an explosive fireball. This fireball may be thrown as per grenade rules and has the same range as an aerodynamic thrown weapon. The explosion has a damage of wyrd or 5 which ever is lower, a blast radius of 2x stamina and a force of strength. </span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T21:10:11-08:00","id":1166239,"title":"","content":"I really like the Blessing <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar600_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"600\" data-vbnamecard=\"600\">HaplessWithDice</a> . My gut says that Burning Wrath is maybe a LITTLE powerful, but... I'm not sure how I'd change it. It's just 1-10 aggravated damage at ground zero. But then again, I suppose it requires both Stamina and Strength for effectiveness. Part of me wonders if maybe it's high level of power would make people hesitate to use it, due to collateral damage and the possibility of friendly fire. My suggestion (made with a lot of thought and referencing Hurt Locker and core) is maybe remove the Force and instead add the Incendiary tag.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-09T07:55:52-08:00","id":1166281,"title":"","content":"<b>Idea: </b><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"309\" data-vbnamecard=\"309\">White Oak Dragon</a>, maybe you will link <a href=\"http://wodcodex.com/wiki/Kiths\" target=\"_blank\">full list of 1E Kiths</a> in Opening Post so people would know what source to look for original Kith - or if their idea has canonical name in 1E. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-09T08:03:01-08:00","id":1166282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1166281#post1166281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Idea: </b><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>, maybe you will link <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://wodcodex.com/wiki/Kiths&amp;quot;]full</a> list of 1E Kiths[/URL] in Opening Post so people would know what source to look for original Kith - or if their idea has canonical name in 1E. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a bad idea. I can't take care of that right now, but I will later. Today, I've got a wedding to attend!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-09T12:51:08-08:00","id":1166323,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, you know, I'm starting to wonder if we shouldn't have a &quot;request list&quot; somewhere so people can look through and see if they have inspiration with something someone else needs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-09T13:10:36-08:00","id":1166326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1166323#post1166323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm, you know, I'm starting to wonder if we shouldn't have a &quot;request list&quot; somewhere so people can look through and see if they have inspiration with something someone else needs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Opening Post seems to be good place - with joined Google Docs for marked those Kiths are done - and link to their post in topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T08:07:53-08:00","id":1166707,"title":"","content":"Another idea <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"309\" data-vbnamecard=\"309\">White Oak Dragon</a> , along with a list of 1st ed Kiths on the first post, but also the page number where they are written up on the topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T12:39:29-08:00","id":1166772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1166707#post1166707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another idea <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> , along with a list of 1st ed Kiths on the first post, but also the page number where they are written up on the topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a bad idea, either, although I'd need to decide how I'd go about it. Mostly because it would be easy for multiple people to update the same kiths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T23:55:00-08:00","id":1166923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1166772#post1166772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not a bad idea, either, although I'd need to decide how I'd go about it. Mostly because it would be easy for multiple people to update the same kiths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Google Docs structure like this:<br /> <br /> Kith 1 - 1E concept sum up<br /> Link-to-post 1<br /> Link-to-post 2<br /> Link-to-post 3<br /> <br /> Kith 2 - 1E concept sum up<br /> Link-to-post 1<br /> Link-to-post 2<br /> <br /> Etc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T00:39:49-08:00","id":1166929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1166923#post1166923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Google Docs structure like this:<br /> <br /> Kith 1 - 1E concept sum up<br /> Link-to-post 1<br /> Link-to-post 2<br /> Link-to-post 3<br /> <br /> Kith 2 - 1E concept sum up<br /> Link-to-post 1<br /> Link-to-post 2<br /> <br /> Etc?</div> </div> </div> </div>With roughly 100 kiths and counting, I think that creating and maintaining such a list would probably require more time than I could spare if I intend to continue writing. If someone else would be willing to do so, though, I could gladly link to it in the initial post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T02:30:13-08:00","id":1166936,"title":"","content":"I think you just really need to start Google Docs and link it to Opening Post - each user could post his own materials, don't they? I can make 1E Kiths list on weekend for you, if need help. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-12-2017, 05:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T07:56:07-08:00","id":1166998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1166936#post1166936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you just really need to start Google Docs and link it to Opening Post - each user could post his own materials, don't they? I can make 1E Kiths list on weekend for you, if need help. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Go for it, Wyrd. That would be quite helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T08:42:18-08:00","id":1167004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1166323#post1166323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm, you know, I'm starting to wonder if we shouldn't have a &amp;quot;request list&amp;quot; somewhere so people can look through and see if they have inspiration with something someone else needs.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you guys do set up such a page, can I request Cleareyes? In the past, I found the Underhill version of that Kith really useful for a character idea I had. However, in trying to homebrew a version to use until the kith book arrives, not only am I having conflicting issues of &quot;keeping it as close to the Underhill version as possible&quot; and &quot;not making it horribly unbalanced,&quot; but I'm also at a loss for the skill portion of the kith due to the closest roll related to it, Perception, not being a skill roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11755-aquatica1000","name":"Aquatica1000","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11755_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T09:12:28-08:00","id":1167010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquatica1000</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1167004#post1167004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you guys do set up such a page, can I request Cleareyes? In the past, I found the Underhill version of that Kith really useful for a character idea I had. However, in trying to homebrew a version to use until the kith book arrives, not only am I having conflicting issues of &amp;quot;keeping it as close to the Underhill version as possible&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;not making it horribly unbalanced,&amp;quot; but I'm also at a loss for the skill portion of the kith due to the closest roll related to it, Perception, not being a skill roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd go with Investigation rolls involving their keenest sense as far as the Skill goes","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T14:11:04-08:00","id":1167125,"title":"","content":"An attempt at the Oracle for a friend, though he doesn't need it, I figure doesn't hurt<br /> <br /> <b>Oracle</b><br /> <br /> <i>The future is an open book, but most are too wise or fearful to open it and gaze upon its pages.</i><br /> <br /> The legends of oracles and seers are ancient ones, and it is said among the first to be Taken were those made to read the future for their Gentry Masters and Mistresses. Some say that is because among those first pledges made with Arcadia, were pacts for the True Fae to bring those who would speak with the voice of the land while listening to the songs of the stars. And so the Oracles first came into being. They were the captive guides that gave Good Folk the edge in the games they play with each other, hobgoblins, or even those who are or were human once.<br /> <br /> The thing that marks all Oracles is their sense of Otherness, even among changelings. They speak with voices that seem not their own, see stars reflected in their eyes even under a clouded sky or in daytime or perhaps their eyes seem cloudy despite their clear vision. They are the old hag Ogre, devouring the unwise. The beautiful Fairest seer bound over a smoking pit. The Wizened scribbling fortunes and truths across every wall or even their own skin. The flight of birds that lands on a Fair One's shoulder or nearby that they might whisper wisdom into his ear. The cave where crash of wave and howl of wind seem to inspire those who listen to the eerie song they give. Or even the Darkling who steals wisdom as seeds and fruits to eat and mindlessly speak out truths in a trance.<br /> <br /> <b>Kith Blessing:</b> When using Persuasion to convince others to believe in the future they saw, the Oracle gets an Exceptional Success on 3 successes instead of 5.<br /> <br /> <i>Eye of Omens:</i>The changeling may spend a point of Glamour, take a single die mild Clarity Attack, and roll Wits + Occult to cause the world to reveal its omens to her. This can take any form from a flight of birds rising up to her breathing onto a mirror or glass and reading the future in the hoarfrost her breath causes. Each success allows the Oracle to ask one of the questions below:<ul><li>Is this path (for herself or others) doomed to ruin?</li> <li>What tools might bring about success on this path?</li> <li>Who has yet to show themselves as part of the current situation?</li> <li>Who can change this path's course most for weal or woe?</li> <li>What can I expect to gain should I succeed?</li> <li>What do I risk losing on failure?</li> </ul>On an exceptional success, the changeling may also ask one of these questions per success over 4:<ul><li>What change can I make to most ensure my victory?</li> <li>What risks must I take to gain more out of my victory?</li> <li>How might I doom my foes the most on my victory?</li> <li>What elements of the situation does no one else notice?</li> </ul>Most Oracles always ask one particular question first. Even if they only have one, it's the answer they always look to. Such is the origin of seers who only speak of doom and ruin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":378,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","user":"haren","date":".  Minor flavor change on advice from non-forum friend 12-12-2017, 05:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T14:54:55-08:00","id":1167143,"title":"","content":"I prepared Kiths list - you just write your version as post link, like in first examples from Beast Seeming Kiths list. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Anyone having link can edit it.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1iBdDevwjjyQvxvc8l2u-e_k-dijNIoCePIMYvRGE_1A/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title el