 /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1iBdDevwjjyQvxvc8l2u-e_k-dijNIoCePIMYvRGE_1A/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Already added my own, though I didn't want to step on anyones' feet by adding theirs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T19:18:48-08:00","id":1167484,"title":"","content":"I have updated the opening post with (hopefully) helpful links. I have also added the first draft of my guide to kith creation, and feedback is quite welcome. The full write-ups of the Windwing and Honeysoul kiths will be added later. For now, I hope this is helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T03:31:14-08:00","id":1167858,"title":"","content":"Do you guys think spending Glamour to see Ghosts is enough for the Gravewright Kith Ability? I was considering adding some sort of bonus to interactions with Ghosts and other kinds of restless dead.<br /> As for the Gravewright Blessing, I thought it would come into effect on Occult actions involving the restless dead.<br /> <br /> Side note: How would you go about doing Dual Kiths in 2e? So many of my character concepts basically revolve around that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T04:43:30-08:00","id":1167869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1167858#post1167858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you guys think spending Glamour to see Ghosts is enough for the Gravewright Kith Ability? I was considering adding some sort of bonus to interactions with Ghosts and other kinds of restless dead.<br /> As for the Gravewright Blessing, I thought it would come into effect on Occult actions involving the restless dead.<br /> <br /> Side note: How would you go about doing Dual Kiths in 2e? So many of my character concepts basically revolve around that.</div> </div> </div> </div>My initial thought on Dual Kith would be to make it a minimum of a three dot Merit, with the drawback of the skill benefit for both kiths only giving an exceptional success on four successes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T08:34:57-08:00","id":1167923,"title":"","content":"Although this one is called Swimmerskin, in the spirit of killing multiple avians with solitary projectiles, it should also be a good stand-in for the Waterborn Elemental kith and the Water-Dweller Ogre kith.<br /> <br /> <b>Swimmerskin</b><br /> <br /> <i>Oh yeah? Why don't you jump in here and say that?</i><br /> <br /> The sea is many things: beautiful, mysterious, dangerous, unfathomably vast. It should come as no surprise that many of the Gentry feel an attraction to the water. Changelings with the Swimmerskin kith may have served their durances as pearl divers on the sea floor of a Fae sea, as the creatures that lurk below the waves, or as the waves themselves.<br /> <br /> A majority of Swimmerskins are at their most comfortable in the water, but many tend to avoid the depths except in case of dire emergency.<br /> <br /> Beast: He might almost be attractive, with his lean body and scintillating green scales, but his webbed fingers and faint fishy smell have made it hard to find romance in the freehold. Not for lack of trying, though.<br /> <br /> Elemental: She constantly looks like she just stepped out of a rainstorm, her hair bedraggled and her soaked clothes leaving wet footprints in her wake. When she smiles, which is rarely, her teeth are tiny chips of beach glass.<br /> <br /> Kith Blessing: When the Swimmerskin uses Athletics to swim, achieving three successes counts as an exceptional success.<br /> <br /> <i>Born to the Water</i>: A Swimmerskin is capable of remaining underwater for far longer than an average mortal. When submerged in water, the Swimmerskin can hold her breath for thirty minutes before making any rolls to avoid drowning. Furthermore, she can spend one Glamour to remain submerged indefinitely; however, this effect ends as soon as her head breaks the surface.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12108-gscrap","name":"gscrap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12108_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T08:45:36-08:00","id":1167925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1167858#post1167858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you guys think spending Glamour to see Ghosts is enough for the Gravewright Kith Ability? I was considering adding some sort of bonus to interactions with Ghosts and other kinds of restless dead.<br /> As for the Gravewright Blessing, I thought it would come into effect on Occult actions involving the restless dead.<br /> <br /> Side note: How would you go about doing Dual Kiths in 2e? So many of my character concepts basically revolve around that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"309\" data-vbnamecard=\"309\">White Oak Dragon</a> on Dual Kiths. As to Gravewight, I think it's far too weak a benefit on its own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-22T21:32:31-08:00","id":1169823,"title":"","content":"I would love feedback on my Woodblood and Cleareyes<br /> <br /> <b>Woodblood</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><i>Did you hear the one about the woodcutter who didn\u2019t know when to stop? Nature always finds a way.</i><br /> Instead of blood, sap slowly works its way through Woodbloods\u2019 veins. Their hair is leaves, their skin bark. Some were taken to be magnificent topiaries, while others were the most beautiful thorned roses. Any Fae can create plants out of glamour and dreams, but the exquisitely solid flesh of a human made into an ornament offers something no dream can. Humans can actually <i>grow</i>. And when they\u2019re trimmed back, they scream in such a delectable way.<br /> <br /> The True Fae seek out humans who are patient and know how to play the long game to achieve their goals to become their prized plants. These are people who are willing to plant the seeds of their success, then watch and tend their development over time. Such a person is sure to offer the juiciest fruits of their labours, the most superb flowers.<br /> To escape Arcadia, some Woodbloods had to literally uproot themselves, deciding on a sudden drastic change in their lives. Others hid their roots deep in the earth, stretching slowly but surely towards the gate of their garden, and from there to the Hedge beyond. There are also those who convinced the hobs tending them to dig them up in exchange for the rarest of fruits that they and the Hedge can provide.<br /> <br /> In Freeholds, Woodbloods make excellent sentinels, as they have the patience necessary to wait and watch for any threat that may come.<br /> <br /> <i>Beast: </i>Leaves smooth all over this changeling like a perfectly cropped topiary or lawn. Branches thrust from their bushy brow, creating towering antlers. Their eyes are two rowan berries, bright red and always open.<br /> <i>Elemental: </i>A shambling mound of fungi and moss that resembles nothing other than if a forest floor decided to get up and walk away.<br /> <br /> <b>Kith Blessing: </b>When the Woodblood uses Survival to identify, scavenge, care for, or harvest plants (including Goblin Fruit), achieving three successes counts as an exceptional success.<br /> <br /> <i>Fade into Foliage</i>: Spend a glamour and roll Stamina + Stealth + Wyrd as a reflexive action to take the form of any plant of at least Size 3. While in this form, the Woodblood is indistinguishable from a natural plant of the chosen type, though observers may notice that a plant has appeared where none was before. As a plant, the Woodblood cannot move, but maintains their full senses. Any attempt to detect them through supernatural means provokes a Clash of Wills. The Woodblood can end this effect at any time as a reflexive action.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Cleareyes</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <i>I see you.</i><br /> When the True Fae seek a Cleareyes, they find people who pay attention to details and notice their physical existence. Tragically, many of these aesthetic souls were locked away in blank room in a tall tower, with a single porthole through which they had to watch for enemies of their Keeper. Others stalked as the foxhounds and hunting birds of True Fae hunters, constantly seeking out the signs of potential prey. Some poor souls were locked away in complete darkness. It wasn\u2019t until they could hear the impossible sound of rocks growing that they could find the hidden exit to their prison.<br /> <br /> <i>Beast: </i>The eyes and feathers of an eagle and the maw and ears of a wolf combine into a human griffin. Massive compound eyes and waving antennae adorn the top of an otherwise normal looking person.<br /> <i>Ogre: </i>Cyclops can smell anyone near them; the Hundred Handed One can see in all directions; The golem of mud and stone can feel the vibrations of footsteps through the floor.<br /> <br /> <b>Kith Blessing: </b>When the Cleareyes rolls Wits + Composure to sense beings who mean them harm, achieving three successes counts as an exceptional success.<br /> <br /> <i>Primal Senses: </i>A Cleareyes can hyper focus their senses. Spend a glamour and roll Wits + Investigation to heighten a specific sense. The Cleareyes may be able to see a license plate clearly from down the street, hear a moth fly by, or smell a particular person in a crowd. The Cleareyes may instead sharpen their awareness of their immediate surroundings and gain an effective 360 degree sensory awareness of stimuli within a short range. They might see a person running up behind them, feel the breezes disturbed by a mosquito taking off their skin, or hear the heartbeat of someone close by. While a Cleareyes has any heightened sense, they risk harming themselves from sudden intense stimuli. They may gain the Blinded, Deafened, or Insensate Tilts in response to a bright flash of light if they have heightened sight, or to a gunshot if they have heightened hearing.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23625,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23625-gedgaroo","user":"gedgaroo","date":". 12-23-2017, 12:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23625-gedgaroo","name":"gedgaroo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T21:26:55-08:00","id":1175084,"title":"","content":"Anyone has an idea for the trickery part of the Treasured Kith from 1E?<br /> <br /> I was thinking to have stealth when immobile as the skill, but updating the blessing is leaving me with a headache.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4990-de_k47","name":"De_K47","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4990_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T07:16:25-08:00","id":1175160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>De_K47</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1175084#post1175084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone has an idea for the trickery part of the Treasured Kith from 1E?<br /> <br /> I was thinking to have stealth when immobile as the skill, but updating the blessing is leaving me with a headache.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you could get away with just reusing the Alabaster Fortitude Blessing, which allows them to, once a scene, pay a glamour to reroll a failed Resistance stat roll (except for certain Clarity-related rolls).<br /> <br /> I would personally take a hint from their role as &quot;valuable possessions&quot; and for that I have two ideas.<br /> <br /> 1) Pay a glamour to gain or upgrade the Striking Looks Merit for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> 2) Pay a glamour to inflict some sort of Obsessed Condition on someone looking at them for the rest of the scene. I'm unsure how the Condition would manifest, but it would be centered on the Changeling and be as risky to use as it is powerful. I was considering Obsession(&quot;Owning&quot; the Treasured), but I'm unsure how the Treasured could semi-reliably turn that goal to their advantage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T07:50:21-08:00","id":1175172,"title":"","content":"Anyone got a recommendation for Coyote's (Winter Masque pg. 107) Blessing? I wanted to make a kith representing them, hyena spirits, Tanuki, Kitsune, etc. Prototyping it under &quot;Laughing Stranger&quot;, but don't want their power being a generic stat boost or attribute discount. So far all I can think of is making their flesh elastic (like with 1e's Mirror Contract: Odd Body) or making a trick where they can fake success to anyone watching them. Attribute + Subterfuge + Wyrd, (Manipulation or Stamina?)<br /> <br /> Please help me. :'3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T08:25:14-08:00","id":1175179,"title":"","content":"The tentative version of the Coyote I jotted down applies its Blessing to uses of Subterfuge to convince someone they are trustworthy, and their power allows them to spend a point of Glamour to improve their impression level by one when starting Social Manuevering. One of these <i>should</i> probably only apply when you first meet someone, but I'm uncertain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T08:29:11-08:00","id":1175180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1175160#post1175160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you could get away with just reusing the Alabaster Fortitude Blessing, which allows them to, once a scene, pay a glamour to reroll a failed Resistance stat roll (except for certain Clarity-related rolls).<br /> <br /> I would personally take a hint from their role as &quot;valuable possessions&quot; and for that I have two ideas.<br /> <br /> 2) Pay a glamour to inflict some sort of Obsessed Condition on someone looking at them for the rest of the scene. I'm unsure how the Condition would manifest, but it would be centered on the Changeling and be as risky to use as it is powerful. I was considering Obsession(&quot;Owning&quot; the Treasured), but I'm unsure how the Treasured could semi-reliably turn that goal to their advantage.</div> </div> </div> </div>This option (2) is the more unique. As to usefulness? Well let's assume the character/player is comfortable with a &quot;grab the spotlight&quot; power. From that point, at least for the subject of the power, they would have a) a lot of trouble focusing on other aspirations and scene objectives--your Treasured becomes the obsessive focus of their attention, to a fully stalker-ish degree if necessary, and b) the subject of the power would be easier for the Treasured to manipulate directly, especially if doing so involves them obtaining &quot;ownership&quot; or control over the Treasured.<br /> <br /> This would also greatly incline the subject to avoid harming the Treasured... and having an on-demand &quot;don't let me get hurt&quot; button (with, ehem, social/freedom drawbacks at least in the short-term) is handy for both players and storytellers.<br /> <br /> So, yes, it's a reliable advantage, assuming the Treasured is keen on worming their way out of such attention on a frequent basis.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T08:42:28-08:00","id":1175183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1175180#post1175180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This option (2) is the more unique. As to usefulness? Well let's assume the character/player is comfortable with a &quot;grab the spotlight&quot; power. From that point, at least for the subject of the power, they would have a) a lot of trouble focusing on other aspirations and scene objectives--your Treasured becomes the obsessive focus of their attention, to a fully stalker-ish degree if necessary, and b) the subject of the power would be easier for the Treasured to manipulate directly, especially if doing so involves them obtaining &quot;ownership&quot; or control over the Treasured.<br /> <br /> This would also greatly incline the subject to avoid harming the Treasured... and having an on-demand &quot;don't let me get hurt&quot; button (with, ehem, social/freedom drawbacks at least in the short-term) is handy for both players and storytellers.<br /> <br /> So, yes, it's a reliable advantage, assuming the Treasured is keen on worming their way out of such attention on a frequent basis.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. You want your precious treasure mint in box","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T13:34:23-08:00","id":1175265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1175179#post1175179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The tentative version of the Coyote I jotted down applies its Blessing to uses of Subterfuge to convince someone they are trustworthy, and their power allows them to spend a point of Glamour to improve their impression level by one when starting Social Manuevering. One of these <i>should</i> probably only apply when you first meet someone, but I'm uncertain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehh, that sound too simple, though. Compared with the other kith blessings we've seen.<br /> <br /> What about this:<br /> <br /> <i>Tall Tale: </i>The Laughing Stranger spends 1 Glamour and rolls Manipulation + Subterfuge + Wyrd vs. Composure + Supernatural Tolerance to weave an elaborate hoax on the target, one that creates and reshapes memories to convincing effect. The changeling has no control on how the target reacts per se, but if he says something as though it were true, the target\u2019s memories are shaped to accommodate it, provided they aren\u2019t blatantly false (it\u2019s raining salmon) or would constitute a breaking point. If someone attempts to convince the target of the truth, or if the target sees evidence that contradicts the tall tale, the target reflexively rolls their Composure + Supernatural Tolerance vs. the changeling\u2019s Wyrd. Success means they break free of the enchantment, either rationalizing it away or coming to their own conclusions on what happened. Otherwise, they gain the Steadfast Condition regarding anything the Laughing Stranger told them. If not negated, the deception lasts as long as the changeling remains present, or till the end of the scene if separated from each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T20:30:31-08:00","id":1175354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1175180#post1175180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This option (2) is the more unique. As to usefulness? Well let's assume the character/player is comfortable with a &amp;quot;grab the spotlight&amp;quot; power. From that point, at least for the subject of the power, they would have a) a lot of trouble focusing on other aspirations and scene objectives--your Treasured becomes the obsessive focus of their attention, to a fully stalker-ish degree if necessary, and b) the subject of the power would be easier for the Treasured to manipulate directly, especially if doing so involves them obtaining &amp;quot;ownership&amp;quot; or control over the Treasured.<br /> <br /> This would also greatly incline the subject to avoid harming the Treasured... and having an on-demand &amp;quot;don't let me get hurt&amp;quot; button (with, ehem, social/freedom drawbacks at least in the short-term) is handy for both players and storytellers.<br /> <br /> So, yes, it's a reliable advantage, assuming the Treasured is keen on worming their way out of such attention on a frequent basis.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe do a mix of the Distracted and Obsessed conditions?<br /> <br /> Irresistible Riches<br /> Spend a Glamour to roll Presence + Persuasion + Wyrd vs Composure + Supernatural Tolerance. On a success, prevent extended action and give a -2 to perception rolls to spot anything else than dangers to the Treasured as the target\u2019s focus is captured. Rolls to prevent harm to the Treasured instead have 9 again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4990-de_k47","name":"De_K47","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4990_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T03:51:00-08:00","id":1175411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>De_K47</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1175354#post1175354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe do a mix of the Distracted and Obsessed conditions?<br /> <br /> Irresistible Riches<br /> Spend a Glamour to roll Presence + Persuasion + Wyrd vs Composure + Supernatural Tolerance. On a success, prevent extended action and give a -2 to perception rolls to spot anything else than dangers to the Treasured as the target\u2019s focus is captured. Rolls to prevent harm to the Treasured instead have 9 again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dunno. But: the One Ring could be a fine example of a Treasured. &quot;My precious!&quot; Indeed.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T07:00:51-08:00","id":1175452,"title":"","content":"Trying to convert the Orphanwretch over and having trouble. Could I get some feedback on this. Also tell me if the concept is kinda offensive to the homeless and if it should be edited.<br /> <br /> <b>Orphanwretch</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Please guvna, you wouldn't turn a boy out on a night like this?</i></span><br /> <br /> The scholars of the Changeling world often wonder why or even how the pitiless Gentry could create creatures who inspire such pity. Their theories are many. Perhaps they were the stars in a morality tale, a spoiled rich kid beaten down into the dirt to teach her a twisted lesson in humility. Perhaps they were homeless folks who stumbled from one big city to another, more fantastical one, but found that the people there were no kinder nor the nights and alleys any warmer. Perhaps they were just left to eke out a living in an endless city after their fairy godmother grew bored of coddling and pampering them. But, the Orphanwretchs know the true reason. They were spys. Taken from the lowest of the low, those whose lives were already so harsh that Arcadia seemed no different or perhaps even better, they were given the gift of wretchedness. No one suspects the filthy street child they take in from the cold to knife them in the back in their sleep; or the old blind pauper of reporting back to their Keeper on potential escapees. For their part, they never went hungry. Many escaped when they could no longer bear the strain of betraying so many a sympathetic face or began to desire more than just survival. Once escaped, they find they can parley their pitiable forms into lives of, if not luxury, then of comfort. But that would all end if their Freeholds knew their true thoughts.<br /> <br /> <i>Elemental</i>: A threadbare teddy bear with a missing ear and soulful button eyes<br /> <br /> <i>Darkling</i>: An impossibly old man, bent over by troubles till he's almost U-shaped and covered in as many ragged layers as he can find.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing</b>: When using Survival or Streetwise to find basic necessities within a city or town, 3 successes counts as an exceptional success.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Whenever another character succeeds in a Social roll against the changeling, he may reflexively spend a point of Glamour to inflict either the Guilty or Leveraged Condition on the character. Doing so also gives the Orphanwretch a number of bonus dice equal to his Wyrd on his next Persuasion or Empathy roll against the character.</span><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> EDIT: Not sure about the blessing. Liked the old one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 01-14-2018, 02:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T10:19:09-08:00","id":1175493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1175265#post1175265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ehh, that sound too simple, though. Compared with the other kith blessings we've seen.<br /> <br /> What about this:<br /> <br /> <i>Tall Tale: </i>The Laughing Stranger spends 1 Glamour and rolls Manipulation + Subterfuge + Wyrd vs. Composure + Supernatural Tolerance to weave an elaborate hoax on the target, one that creates and reshapes memories to convincing effect. The changeling has no control on how the target reacts per se, but if he says something as though it were true, the target\u2019s memories are shaped to accommodate it, provided they aren\u2019t blatantly false (it\u2019s raining salmon) or would constitute a breaking point. If someone attempts to convince the target of the truth, or if the target sees evidence that contradicts the tall tale, the target reflexively rolls their Composure + Supernatural Tolerance vs. the changeling\u2019s Wyrd. Success means they break free of the enchantment, either rationalizing it away or coming to their own conclusions on what happened. Otherwise, they gain the Steadfast Condition regarding anything the Laughing Stranger told them. If not negated, the deception lasts as long as the changeling remains present, or till the end of the scene if separated from each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems a bit more complicated and less intuitive than what I'd go with, but it's a fairly curious idea. Go with it if it pleases you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T10:22:11-08:00","id":1175496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1175493#post1175493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That seems a bit more complicated and less intuitive than what I'd go with, but it's a fairly curious idea. Go with it if it pleases you!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I don't want it to be too complicated... suggestions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T10:32:32-08:00","id":1175498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1175452#post1175452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trying to convert the Orphanwretch over and having trouble. Could I get some feedback on this. Also tell me if the concept is kinda offensive to the homeless and if it should be edited.<br /> <br /> <b>Orphanwretch</b></div> </div> </div> </div>The description seems to only lightly brush homeless people; seems fair. <br /> <br /> Their power set is utterly terrifying in its laser-like focus. We will never look at the little flower-girl on the corner the same, again....<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T10:41:19-08:00","id":1175500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1175498#post1175498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The description seems to only lightly brush homeless people; seems fair.<br /> <br /> Their power set is utterly terrifying in its laser-like focus. We will never look at the little flower-girl on the corner the same, again....<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks. A Fae or even a Court Monarch with a spy network made of these guys and Sprites would be pretty scary, wouldn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T14:01:15-08:00","id":1175556,"title":"","content":"Welp, next semester doesn't start for another week, no sign of my EMT license and I'm in a kith-creating mood. If anyone has any kiths they'd love to port over but they don't have the time, ask for them here. There's too many for me to choose from even in the core.<br /> <br /> EDIT: One at a time though, please. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 01-12-2018, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-13T11:33:24-08:00","id":1175809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1175452#post1175452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trying to convert the Orphanwretch over and having trouble. Could I get some feedback on this. Also tell me if the concept is kinda offensive to the homeless and if it should be edited.<br /> <br /> <b>Orphanwretch</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Look kid, I'm sorry. No, no, don't cry. I shouldn't have said that. Please, don't cry. Come on, I'll buy you dinner</i></span><br /> <br /> The scholars of the Changeling world often wonder why or even how the pitiless Gentry could create creatures who inspire such pity. Their theories are many. Perhaps they were the stars in a morality tale, a spoiled rich kid beaten down into the dirt to teach her a twisted lesson in humility. Perhaps they were homeless folks who stumbled from one big city to another, more fantastical one, but found that the people there were no kinder nor the nights and alleys any warmer. Perhaps they were just left to eke out a living in an endless city after their fairy godmother grew bored of coddling and pampering them. But, the Orphanwretchs know the true reason. They were spys. Taken from the lowest of the low, those whose lives were already so harsh that Arcadia seemed no different or perhaps even better, they were given the gift of wretchedness. No one suspects the filthy street child they take in from the cold to knife them in the back in their sleep; or the old blind pauper of reporting back to their Keeper on potential escapees. For their part, they never went hungry. Many escaped when they could no longer bear the strain of betraying so many a sympathetic face or began to desire more than just survival. Once escaped, they find they can parley their pitiable forms into lives of, if not luxury, then of comfort. But that would all end if their Freeholds knew their true thoughts.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing</b>: When using Subterfuge to convince someone they are harmless or in need of help, achieving 3 successes counts as a exceptional success.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Whenever another character succeeds in a Social roll against the changeling, he may reflexively spend a point of Glamour to inflict either the Guilty or Leveraged Condition on the character. Doing so also gives the Orphanwretch a number of bonus dice equal to his Wyrd on his next Persuasion or Subterfuge roll against the character.</span><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Looking pretty good so far. I'd change the quote, since the quotes all seem to come from a member of the kith in this version. You'll also need to add the two Seeming descriptions. I would consider tweaking the blessing a little as well, mostly so that their skill trick doesn't also boost the trickery aspect. I'd probably change one of the Subterfuges to Empathy, personally. Still, you're off to a great start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-13T14:03:45-08:00","id":1175839,"title":"","content":"Thanks, but why Empathy? Thats more for reading other people when they are not trying to hide stuff. Im not sure how they'd use <br /> <br /> Anyway, what if i changed the blessing to be getting exceptional success at 3 for rolls that help with basic survival on city and town streets, have that extra survivability be the carrot that the Gentry offered them in exchange for spy work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-13T16:45:58-08:00","id":1175862,"title":"","content":"Here's a kith I've been working on for a bit; let me know what you guys think of it. I was thinking of making an effect that didn't require a Glamour to activate, though I made sure there was a thematic downside for it. Not sure if I should allow it to work in scenarios outside of solo-investigations.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Janus</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><i>It was easy for me to solve. I just had to get into the right mindsets.</i><br /> The Gentry would never admit that some things baffle them, be it games, locks, people or even riddles. Their minds are byzantine, but sometimes it takes a simple fact to trip them up and have them look for something that isn\u2019t obvious. Usually they say they\u2019re too busy to deal with such matters, or that they\u2019re too bored to handle such a simple thing. Sometimes they\u2019re telling the truth.<br /> <br /> Whatever the reason, should such a situation arise, they have but to call upon a Janus to handle matters. Janus were people who had minds designed to deconstruct problems, be it a person\u2019s motivations, a logic puzzle, a riddle or even just what was gumming up clockwork. They may not have been the best at solving those problems, but understanding them was never an issue. The Gentry simply took what was there and divided it, optimizing each mind to handle different aspects while still being the same whole.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, with the way the Gentry operate, it\u2019s not entirely clear if this is the case for every Janus. Some Changelings claim to have seen Gentry take a person\u2019s mind and mix it with anothers, creating two Changelings who were not themselves but worked better than before. Others have whispered of seeing a single mind be divided and given multiple bodies, filling in the empty spaces with tomes, wax recordings and bits of miscellaneous junk. More than one Janus has been kept up at night with worry they were as much a creation of Arcadia as a Fetch, particularly by those without a Fetch to find.<br /> <br /> Regardless of how they were made, a Janus was meant to do the work of many in a short amount of time, and they did so well. However, mental fortitude is a common issue among the multi-minded. As with a roommate, sibling or even a spouse, living in the same place as someone can make one painfully aware of the other\u2019s foibles, bringing out arguments and venom. Janus don\u2019t have the option of leaving the room when they get to their minds start arguing. Meditation helps, but only so far.<br /> <br /> <i>Beast:</i> He works as a bodyguard to make ends meet, sniffing out people as safe or hostile with all three of his noses. When people see him talk to his shoulders, unable to see past the mask, they think he's either talking to a microphone or simply insane. They don't see the burning cerebus arguing with himself.<br /> <br /> <i>Wizened:</i> Her head is an upright reel, the film showing different expressions of her face. When her emotions change, the reel spins and stops on the appropriate one. She\u2019s pleasant, but those close to her can hear the whispers of the film underneath the clicking of plastic gears.<br /> <br /> <i>Fairest:</i> She was a spy for her Keeper during their meetings with other Gentry, acting as a harlequin as she observed them. Nobody has ever seen her face change expression as it is always obscured by something in the transition, usually by the mirror she talks to. Mortals take her as eccentric; the Lost see her as borderline insane.<br /> <br /> <b>Kith Blessing:</b> When the Janus uses Investigation to determine a character's motive, achieving three successes counts as an exceptional success.<br /> <i>Take Two:</i> Janus are never alone when investigating, always having two (or more) minds about anything they find. During an investigation a Janus can do a Teamwork action by themselves, rolling their die pool and then using any successes in that roll as extra dice in the ensuing investigation. Doing so results in the Janus gaining the Confused, Dissociation or Disoriented condition at the end of the scene, as their heads start squabbling about the results and how they were obtained.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-13T19:16:52-08:00","id":1175888,"title":"","content":"Would Brawl or Weaponry work better as the Kith blessing for the Razorhands? I've been trying to homebrew a 2E conversion for them, but I can't seem to decide the right skill for the job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11755-aquatica1000","name":"Aquatica1000","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11755_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-13T19:27:41-08:00","id":1175890,"title":"","content":"What do natural weapons use for a die pool?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-13T19:29:47-08:00","id":1175891,"title":"","content":"Typically Strength + Brawl, if I remember correctly. I guess I've been overthinking stuff again, sorry... -///-'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11755-aquatica1000","name":"Aquatica1000","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11755_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-13T21:27:08-08:00","id":1175909,"title":"","content":"No need to apologize; it was a good question to ponder over. However, I was reminded that it's effectively a natural weapon, and so it would work with what a natural weapon uses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-14T05:17:05-08:00","id":1175960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1175839#post1175839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks, but why Empathy? Thats more for reading other people when they are not trying to hide stuff. Im not sure how they'd use <br /> <br /> Anyway, what if i changed the blessing to be getting exceptional success at 3 for rolls that help with basic survival on city and town streets, have that extra survivability be the carrot that the Gentry offered them in exchange for spy work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Empathy is useful for figuring out how people tick. You can use it to figure out someone's motives, to understand what they really desire, regardless of what they claim. If they're hiding something, Empathy might not trick them into revealing what it is, but it could be used to pick up on the fact there is something they don't want known. From there, convincing them that you're a kindred spirit can help to draw them out.<br /> <br /> Giving them a Survival skill trick for urban environments isn't a bad idea, and it would take care of the Subterfuge issue I mentioned. I'd say that the trick was probably incidental to the job rather than a payment for it. I could see a lot of Orphanwretches doing the job simply because their Keeper is &quot; the only one that ever really cared about them&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-14T10:18:44-08:00","id":1175997,"title":"","content":"And I finally finished the write-up. I just hope it looks good.<br /> <br /> <b>Razorhand</b><br /> <i>The Fae wanted me to be a mindless weapon, to kill whatever they want. Well, no more. This blade is mine, and I'll choose whose blood to spill.</i><br /> When the Fae make a Razorhand, they\u2019re looking for someone who can kill with ease, whether as an assassin striking from the shadows or a bodyguard cutting down those who stand in their master\u2019s way. To that end, the Razorhands are taken by forced and altered \u2013 oftentimes via the painful implementation of some type of blade into their hands and fingers \u2013 only to then be used as living weapons. It is often with these skills that the changelings often slip their captors.<br /> Once away from Arcadia, though, the Razorhands still must figure out what to do with their newfound freedom. There are plenty who turn to the summer court, eager to turn their combat skill to good use, but there are others still who use their skills to strike fear. And then there are those who, remorseful for those they have slain, turn to pacifism to atone for their sins.<br /> <i>Beast:</i> He\u2019s got the slitted eyes and striped pelt of a tiger, as well as the cocky attitude befitting one. When the going gets tough, though, he\u2019s quick to demonstrate to his foes that his claws aren\u2019t just meant to look pretty.<br /> <i>Elemental: </i>She is a representation of metal as a means of violence, with wiry hair and an expression one aggravation away from staring daggers. Sharp blades extend out of her hands almost naturally, as if she were born from them.<br /> <b>Blessing: </b> When a Razorhand charges at a target and makes an unarmed attack, three successes on the Brawl roll counts as an exceptional success.<br /> <i>Aim to Maim:</i> The Razorhand can choose to inflict lethal damage with his unarmed weapon (if the Changeling can already inflict lethal damage with unarmed attacks via abilities such as the Beast Seeming, it adds to the base damage by 1). In addition, by spending a point of Glamour and rolling Strength + Weaponry, the Razorhand can choose to automatically inflict one of the following Tilts in the next successful unarmed attack: Arm Wrack, Blinded, Deafened, or Leg Wrack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11755-aquatica1000","name":"Aquatica1000","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11755_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-14T11:26:06-08:00","id":1176008,"title":"","content":"<b>New Kith: Laughing Stranger</b><br /> <div align=\"center\"><i>Of course you know me! We went to high school together, remember? Exactly, been best buds ever since you got wasted that one time at the mall. Can I come in? </i></div> Trust is a hard thing to come by, even among changelings. The Gentry knows this more than most, and so they mold Laughing Strangers to test their own wits, or perhaps fool other changelings into believing only what they want them to. Paranoia will sometimes drive a Keeper to kidnap a mortal terrible at spinning tales, if only to ensure they aren't outmatched, or they make one by accident from authors, actors and poets in hopes of hearing elaborate stories and recitations thereof.<br /> While pledges might keep them honest, Laughing Strangers make their way by misleading others with elaborate cons that play on people's assumptions. They\u2019re the anansis, the shadowy confidants, animal-headed tricksters who weave tall tales about the sky falling. To a Laughing Stranger, fast-talking and confusing rhetoric are both artform and a means of survival. It\u2019s often how they escaped Arcadia, using the chaos spurred on by a guest turned rival, or wooing the guards with altered memories of courtship. Not that all Laughing Strangers are liars, they're just very convincing, even to the point of one's mind playing tricks on them to support the changeling's position. Something about them just makes it easy to open up to, making them ideal confessors and spies.<br /> <br /> <i>Beast: </i>She\u2019s got the head and fur of a fox, or was it a coyote? Her tail swishes when she\u2019s got her eye on someone special, and her dancing\u2019s as wild as the stories she tells. <br /> <br /> <i>Darkling:</i> Lanky fellow in the corner, wears a hoodie. Got a half-meter long, purple tongue coming out of his mouth. It\u2019s why he prefers whispering, easier to hide behind those bright white teeth of his.<br /> <br /> <b>Kith Blessing:</b> The Laughing Stranger attains Exceptional Success on 3 successes rather than 5 when using Subterfuge to convince someone of their trustworthiness.<br /> <br /> <i>Tall Tale:</i> The Laughing Stranger spends 1 Glamour and rolls Manipulation + Subterfuge + Wyrd vs. Composure + Supernatural Tolerance to weave an elaborate hoax on the target, one that creates and reshapes memories to convincing effect. The changeling has no control on how the target reacts per se, but if he says something as though it were true, the target\u2019s memories are shaped to accommodate it, provided they aren\u2019t blatantly false (it\u2019s raining salmon) or would constitute a breaking point. If someone attempts to convince the target of the truth, or if the target sees evidence that contradicts the tall tale, the target reflexively rolls their Composure + Supernatural Tolerance vs. the changeling\u2019s Wyrd. Success means they break free of the enchantment, either rationalizing it away or coming to their own conclusions on what happened. Otherwise, they gain the Steadfast Condition regarding anything the Laughing Stranger told them. If not negated, the deception lasts as long as the changeling remains present, or till the end of the scene if they remain separated.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T17:58:58-08:00","id":1177472,"title":"","content":"Would it be too overpowered to have a kith based on manipulating luck so they could add or subtract others dicepools? Not really sure how such a concept might be statted out other than making them equal to successes rolled on a skill roll as part of invoking up to a certain limit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5413-icefyer","name":"Icefyer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T18:29:26-08:00","id":1177480,"title":"","content":"Considering that there's a contract that can do that, and it's limited to being used on a target once a day before it backfires, that may be a bit of an issue. If you want something to manipulate rolls, maybe being allowed to reroll a particular roll instead of the die pools?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T18:32:46-08:00","id":1177481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1177480#post1177480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that there's a contract that can do that, and it's limited to being used on a target once a day before it backfires, that may be a bit of an issue. If you want something to manipulate rolls, maybe being allowed to reroll a particular roll instead of the die pools?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh? How might that work? Because the previous 2e playtest stuff had Witchtooth that could subtract from dicepools, so I was wondering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5413-icefyer","name":"Icefyer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-20T23:02:49-08:00","id":1177783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Icefyer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1177481#post1177481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh? How might that work? Because the previous 2e playtest stuff had Witchtooth that could subtract from dicepools, so I was wondering.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was not what it did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T06:46:37-08:00","id":1177834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1177783#post1177783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was not what it did.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was absolutely what it did. 8-Again on Occult rolls and the ability to point at someone or look them in the eye, roll Wits + Occult - Resolve, and curse the next use of a named Skill or action with a -Wyrd penalty such that its failure gave the Witchtooth a point of Willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 01-21-2018, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T12:23:24-08:00","id":1178145,"title":"","content":"So with the help of this forum and the changeling Discord: <br /> <br /> Fatebreaker: When determining omens and portents not related to their blessing, such as the use of contracts related to manipulating fortune and the future, 3 instead of 5.<br /> <br /> The user may roll Wits + Occult and spend a glamour to speak a prediction affecting a skill to the target of their choice, such as &quot;When you attempt to heal Mr. Bunsen, his wounds will not be as deep as you first believe&quot;, allowing allies or forcing an enemy to reroll the related skill the first time it is rolled, some time within the scene and take the better / worse result accordingly. Rerolls do not guarentee success as predicting the future and luck are fickle, slippery things at best, and if a roll is reduced to a chance die it is ineligible to be rerolled and they do not stack. In the case of an extended action the user may choose which roll, such as the medicine check for Mr. Bunsen above, benefits from the reroll. If they don't use the blessed / cursed skill before the scene is up, the glamour is still spent and the blessing / curse is wasted.<br /> <br /> Any thought?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5413-icefyer","name":"Icefyer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T15:18:35-08:00","id":1178227,"title":"","content":"Maybe a restriction that Fatebreaker can only be used once per scene? This would make it cheaper to use than Changing Fortunes, but at the same time more limited.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, I like it; the fact you specified that the skill is rerolled the first time it is rolled, that it works differently for an extended roll, but that chance dice are excluded from its effects. I also like you specified that the Kith Blessing works towards omens and portents not related to their blessing, though I'd specify that it uses Occult for that. Overall this would be a Kith that the Autumn court would covet greatly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T08:03:52-08:00","id":1178435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1178227#post1178227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe a restriction that Fatebreaker can only be used once per scene? This would make it cheaper to use than Changing Fortunes, but at the same time more limited.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, I like it; the fact you specified that the skill is rerolled the first time it is rolled, that it works differently for an extended roll, but that chance dice are excluded from its effects. I also like you specified that the Kith Blessing works towards omens and portents not related to their blessing, though I'd specify that it uses Occult for that. Overall this would be a Kith that the Autumn court would covet greatly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True, but it's also essentially like the Wizened bonus for Changing Fortunes as a kith blessing, so it has no ability to manipulate dice pools or change the critical success rate of the roll itself, it just gives another attempt and it might take up your action for the turn, almost like giving up one of your own rolls to allow / force someone to reroll theirs. I had debated allowing the reroll for any of the particular skill, like if they botched the second time rolling Medicine they could reroll that one, but it seemed a bit strong. And it's nowhere near as strong as the Mage spell that lets you do the same thing, but for an entire scene of rerolls, so I figured it made an appropriate kith blessing if it only applied once, and there's a werewolf merit which lets you do it but only in very specific circumstances, so it's stronger than a merit. Oddly enough allowing rerolls is something that happens extremely rarely and almost nothing actually takes advantage of it.<br /> <br /> And considering Changing Fortunes is only once per game session but at higher levels of skill could easily add 8+ extra dice if you succeed well enough or reduce the crit success rating to a single success AND forcing the reroll if you take the Wiz bonus for a grand total of 1 XP for non-Wiz, that's a rather powerful contract!<br /> <br /> Also, how might you balance a potential dual kith, should a player want that merit back?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5413,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5413-icefyer","user":"Icefyer","date":". 01-23-2018, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5413-icefyer","name":"Icefyer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T11:13:44-08:00","id":1178871,"title":"","content":"Not a kith, but I thought I'd make something of a supplemental goblin fruit for Gristlegrinders.<br /> <br /> <i><b>New Goblin Fruit: Gobblepot</b></i><br /> Found in swamps, marshes, or in the cavities of long dead hob goblins, Gobblepot takes the shape of a rotund, orange pitcher plant with blue insides. When filled with water, and properly boiled, the liquid mixes with the juice to create a single, magical draught. When taken, this incandescent blue liquid covers the walls of the changeling\u2019s stomach, forming a spongy material that absorbs the effects of any ingested materials thereafter. Conditions and Tilts caused by poisons, orally taken drugs, even other goblin fruit are rendered inert. However, after a number of hours equal to the changeling\u2019s Stamina + Wyrd, they are forced to regurgitate the contents of their stomach, thus ending the effect. Everything remains dry provided no other liquids were consumed (repeat-users have been noted to suffer dry mouth and nausea).<br /> Interestingly enough, Gobblepot has an additional effect on Gristlegrinders. While active, anyone swallowed whole by the Gristlegrinder\u2019s kith blessing is protected from the usual stomach acid, instead becoming more of a passenger or mobile prisoner. This does not protect them from anything the Gristlegrinder swallows <i>afterwards,</i> but few complain about not being digested, especially after their gracious host finally spits them back out. The Gristlegrinder can release such guests as an instant action, with their maw expanding as it would normally when swallowing with their kith blessing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":974,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","user":"MrParaduo","date":". 01-24-2018, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T02:11:31-08:00","id":1180369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1178871#post1178871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not a kith, but I thought I'd make something of a supplemental goblin fruit for Gristlegrinders.<br /> <br /> <i><b>New Goblin Fruit: Gobblepot</b></i><br /> Found in swamps, marshes, or in the cavities of long dead hob goblins, Gobblepot takes the shape of a rotund, orange pitcher plant with blue insides. When filled with water, and properly boiled, the liquid mixes with the juice to create a single, magical draught. When taken, this incandescent blue liquid covers the walls of the changeling\u2019s stomach, forming a spongy material that absorbs the effects of any ingested materials thereafter. Conditions and Tilts caused by poisons, orally taken drugs, even other goblin fruit are rendered inert. However, after a number of hours equal to the changeling\u2019s Stamina + Wyrd, they are forced to regurgitate the contents of their stomach, thus ending the effect. Everything remains dry provided no other liquids were consumed (repeat-users have been noted to suffer dry mouth and nausea).<br /> Interestingly enough, Gobblepot has an additional effect on Gristlegrinders. While active, anyone swallowed whole by the Gristlegrinder\u2019s kith blessing is protected from the usual stomach acid, instead becoming more of a passenger or mobile prisoner. This does not protect them from anything the Gristlegrinder swallows <i>afterwards,</i> but few complain about not being digested, especially after their gracious host finally spits them back out. The Gristlegrinder can release such guests as an instant action, with their maw expanding as it would normally when swallowing with their kith blessing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It may not be a kith, but it's certainly a fine goblin fruit. I absolutely adore it, and it made its first appearance in my games tonight. Well done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T03:25:42-08:00","id":1180372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1180369#post1180369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It may not be a kith, but it's certainly a fine goblin fruit. I absolutely adore it, and it made its first appearance in my games tonight. Well done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aww, thank you! ^_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T01:34:25-08:00","id":1180642,"title":"","content":"Hey guys and gals, I'm working on a conversion for the Author Kith and I'm hoping the combined wisdom of the forums will be able to help me out. So far the exceptional success bonus was easy (ES's are brought down to 3 instead of 5 whenever the changeling rolls to use expression for writing) but I can't come up with the kiths trickery. I'm leaning towards convincing people through writing, but that doesn't seem quite right. Other options I'm considering are letting her understand the meaning of any piece of writing or maybe let her have 9 or even 8 again on writing rolls.<br /> <br /> Thoughts, anyone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7372-lady-gray","name":"Lady Gray","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7372_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T06:23:21-08:00","id":1180688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lady Gray</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1180642#post1180642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey guys and gals, I'm working on a conversion for the Author Kith and I'm hoping the combined wisdom of the forums will be able to help me out. So far the exceptional success bonus was easy (ES's are brought down to 3 instead of 5 whenever the changeling rolls to use expression for writing) but I can't come up with the kiths trickery. I'm leaning towards convincing people through writing, but that doesn't seem quite right. Other options I'm considering are letting her understand the meaning of any piece of writing or maybe let her have 9 or even 8 again on writing rolls.<br /> <br /> Thoughts, anyone?</div> </div> </div> </div>The purpose of writing is to convince or to convey or to evoke a state of mind or emotion. With that in mind, I could see an Author Kith using the written word to create or enhance emotion beyond what mere words (even with critical successes) could produce. You could also flip it, and let the character read to understand exactly what the emotions and state of mind was for the writer when a text was penned, for instance.<br /> <br /> Obviously using writing to create states of mind [Conditions, Tilts] and emotion are... useful... to Changelings, no?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T07:55:16-08:00","id":1180711,"title":"","content":"Hmm. The ability to understand context even in text, one of the most context-free media ever. Sounds useful. Frankly, sounds like a good Author would be an even better literature professor or reviewer. Plus, very resistant to tragic misunderstandings from sarcastic texts or illicitly read diary entries, though the added resistance would lead to more stubbornness when they inevitably do end up getting the wrong impression from their literary psychometry, which makes for good stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T11:00:36-08:00","id":1180813,"title":"","content":"You could also go with &quot;subtext&quot;, allowing them to write hidden messages into their work (or even existing work?). An offensive bit of graffiti could warn all changelings of a dangerous gate into the Hedge, for instance. That's probably what I would do if I was updating them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T03:50:44-08:00","id":1181961,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Author</u></b><br /> <i>They say the pen is mightier than the sword. That's garbage of course-I wouldn't bring a pen to a sword fight. No, the trick of it is, a pen in the right hand can make sure your enemy can't even summon up the will to lift their sword in the first place. Then you can drive the pen through their eye, if you really insist on getting physical.</i><br /> <br /> The gentry are ego personified. They revel in self aggrandizement-how can you not, they say, when the very ground you walk on thanks you for the honor? But of course, being great is never enough-people have to know you're great. Of course you can tell them yourself, but that's rather gauche now, isn't it? No, far better to have someone else there to tell everybody how great you are. Or perhaps the Keeper is bored. A childlike true fae, easily distracted, needs a good flow of new diversions, and what better way to divert a being of madness and story than more stories?<br /> <br /> And that's where the authors come in. Humans often chosen for their creativity, they were plucked from their world and dragged through the thorns, then made to use the blood from their freshly torn wounds as ink to write stories to please their Keepers. Some record the feats of their true fae master, some create stories from their own imaginations to delight and enchant. <br /> <br /> Once they've returned ironside, authors retain their preternatural capacity for storytelling, able to weave tales to astonish and horrify and delight with ease. These changelings are the ones most likely to talk about their durance, filling in the blanks with dramatic detail; sometimes they cleave as close to the truth of their memories as they can, sometimes they inject spectacular falsehoods of one sort or another, but either way, they've found that a story shared is a burden halved.<br /> <br /> <i>Beast</i>: This changeling looks vaguely like a crow, with black feathers and large, obsidian eyes. They seem to hunch forward, scrawling what they see in one of a half-dozen journals they keep on their person at all times, each one for a specific kind of story divided in a way that only they know about.<br /> <br /> <i>Elemental</i>: This changeling seems to be made of wood and parchment, words inked over their skin, shifting and changing constantly. They sit in their one spot at the bar, silent and still, until someone sends them over a drink and asks for a story. Then they become as animated and energetic as anyone could hope to be.<br /> <br /> <i>Kith blessing: </i>When the changeling makes an expression roll that involves writing, they only need three successes instead of five for an exceptional success.<br /> <br /> <i>Read between the lines</i>: More than any other kith, the authors know that the most important things are the things that go unsaid. The changeling can spend a point of glamour and make a wits+expression roll to either; imbue a piece of work with the ability to evoke a specific emotion in anyone who reads it (the reader can trigger a clash of wills to resist the effect) or; they can understand the subtext of any one piece of writing that they read. Each new piece of writing requires a new instance of initiating this blessing.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Alright, here's my crack at the author kith. Do you think the kith blessing might be overpowered? Having essentially two abilities could be a bit much, but I thought that given they're fairly situational, that might balance them out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7372-lady-gray","name":"Lady Gray","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7372_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T03:38:26-08:00","id":1182219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lady Gray</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1181961#post1181961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>Author</u></b><br /> <i>They say the pen is mightier than the sword. That's garbage of course-I wouldn't bring a pen to a sword fight. No, the trick of it is, a pen in the right hand can make sure your enemy can't even summon up the will to lift their sword in the first place. Then you can drive the pen through their eye, if you really insist on getting physical.</i><br /> <br /> The gentry are ego personified. They revel in self aggrandizement-how can you not, they say, when the very ground you walk on thanks you for the honor? But of course, being great is never enough-people have to know you're great. Of course you can tell them yourself, but that's rather gauche now, isn't it? No, far better to have someone else there to tell everybody how great you are. Or perhaps the Keeper is bored. A childlike true fae, easily distracted, needs a good flow of new diversions, and what better way to divert a being of madness and story than more stories?<br /> <br /> And that's where the authors come in. Humans often chosen for their creativity, they were plucked from their world and dragged through the thorns, then made to use the blood from their freshly torn wounds as ink to write stories to please their Keepers. Some record the feats of their true fae master, some create stories from their own imaginations to delight and enchant. <br /> <br /> Once they've returned ironside, authors retain their preternatural capacity for storytelling, able to weave tales to astonish and horrify and delight with ease. These changelings are the ones most likely to talk about their durance, filling in the blanks with dramatic detail; sometimes they cleave as close to the truth of their memories as they can, sometimes they inject spectacular falsehoods of one sort or another, but either way, they've found that a story shared is a burden halved.<br /> <br /> <i>Beast</i>: This changeling looks vaguely like a crow, with black feathers and large, obsidian eyes. They seem to hunch forward, scrawling what they see in one of a half-dozen journals they keep on their person at all times, each one for a specific kind of story divided in a way that only they know about.<br /> <br /> <i>Elemental</i>: This changeling seems to be made of wood and parchment, words inked over their skin, shifting and changing constantly. They sit in their one spot at the bar, silent and still, until someone sends them over a drink and asks for a story. Then they become as animated and energetic as anyone could hope to be.<br /> <br /> <i>Kith blessing: </i>When the changeling makes an expression roll that involves writing, they only need three successes instead of five for an exceptional success.<br /> <br /> <i>Read between the lines</i>: More than any other kith, the authors know that the most important things are the things that go unsaid. The changeling can spend a point of glamour and make a wits+expression roll to either; imbue a piece of work with the ability to evoke a specific emotion in anyone who reads it (the reader can trigger a clash of wills to resist the effect) or; they can understand the subtext of any one piece of writing that they read. Each new piece of writing requires a new instance of initiating this blessing.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Alright, here's my crack at the author kith. Do you think the kith blessing might be overpowered? Having essentially two abilities could be a bit much, but I thought that given they're fairly situational, that might balance them out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, how about expanding the eased exceptional to both writing mundanely and reading writings (which would include reading subtext and other authors\u2019 intentions), and the Trickery supernaturally imbuing the Author\u2019s own writings with emotions (represented by Conditions)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T17:11:26-08:00","id":1183432,"title":"","content":"Not so much a conversion, but I had an idea for a Kith known as a Deadeye - they're basically sharpshooters among Changelings, designed to always be armed and dangerous even with an empty gun. I don't know what to make for their Kith Blessing though. Their Trickery is below:<br /> <br /> A Bullet With Your Name On It: A Deadeye's gun is always loaded. By spending a Glamour and successfully rolling Presence + Firearms, any gun a Deadeye is holding is instantly loaded with ammunition appropriate for its type. Even if the firearm is missing its magazine, it is considered loaded to its maximum capacity. These bullets are unique to the Changeling, being composed of materials such as crystal, ice or even something like compacted star dust and do the same damage as normal ammunition. Any un-fired bullets dissolve into nothing at the end of the scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T18:00:19-08:00","id":1183448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1183432#post1183432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not so much a conversion, but I had an idea for a Kith known as a Deadeye - they're basically sharpshooters among Changelings, designed to always be armed and dangerous even with an empty gun. I don't know what to make for their Kith Blessing though. Their Trickery is below:<br /> <br /> A Bullet With Your Name On It: A Deadeye's gun is always loaded. By spending a Glamour and successfully rolling Presence + Firearms, any gun a Deadeye is holding is instantly loaded with ammunition appropriate for its type. Even if the firearm is missing its magazine, it is considered loaded to its maximum capacity. These bullets are unique to the Changeling, being composed of materials such as crystal, ice or even something like compacted star dust and do the same damage as normal ammunition. Any un-fired bullets dissolve into nothing at the end of the scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thought it's worth mentioning there's a Brothers Grimm story involving siblings who develop impossible skills and return to show off to their father. To test the marksman son, the father put five eggs on a table: One on each corner, and one in the center. The marksman shot all five eggs with one bullet &quot;using a special gunpowder for shooting around corners.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T18:03:12-08:00","id":1183450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1183448#post1183448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thought it's worth mentioning there's a Brothers Grimm story involving siblings who develop impossible skills and return to show off to their father. To test the marksman son, the father put five eggs on a table: One on each corner, and one in the center. The marksman shot all five eggs with one bullet &quot;using a special gunpowder for shooting around corners.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>There can be multiple sharpshooter kiths - there's bound to be overlap, or regional varients on various kiths, just as there are repeats. I just like the idea of a Changeling being able to get into a firefight, have an empty gun, and then wait for their target to casually walk up to them only for the Changeling to use their Kith blessing and then shoot the surprised target...or simply for more dakka without having to reload casually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T12:49:16-08:00","id":1183666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1183432#post1183432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not so much a conversion, but I had an idea for a Kith known as a Deadeye - they're basically sharpshooters among Changelings, designed to always be armed and dangerous even with an empty gun. I don't know what to make for their Kith Blessing though. Their Trickery is below:<br /> <br /> A Bullet With Your Name On It: A Deadeye's gun is always loaded. By spending a Glamour and successfully rolling Presence + Firearms, any gun a Deadeye is holding is instantly loaded with ammunition appropriate for its type. Even if the firearm is missing its magazine, it is considered loaded to its maximum capacity. These bullets are unique to the Changeling, being composed of materials such as crystal, ice or even something like compacted star dust and do the same damage as normal ammunition. Any un-fired bullets dissolve into nothing at the end of the scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nicely done. I like what you did with their Trickery. I actually wrote a Deadeye kith for the Underhill version, though their blessing was considerably different than yours despite sharing the name and sharpshooter concept. Their 2E conversion is quite different as well, although I can't share that yet, as I sent them to Meghan as a writing sample.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T13:33:23-08:00","id":1183686,"title":"","content":"Why not just make their blessing be exceptional success at 3 on all Firearms rolls more complex than just shooting at a wide-open, stationary or predictably moving target, with the added caveat that with an exceptional success, they can make seemingly impossible trick shots?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Not sure if Discreet Conjuration is in 2e but if it is, the Trickery is a little redundant out-of-character. Sure, it could reload a bigger gun, but Discreet Conjuration can basically give you as many pistols as you have glamour, and it doesn't sound like it would be rolled in 2e.<br /> <br /> EDIT 2: Never mind, looked closer and realized that Discreet Conjuration costs a lot more to cast than this Trickery at 2 Glamour + 1 Willpower. Still think that More Dakka is a little out of them for a trick shooter, if that's what the flavor's supposed to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 02-08-2018, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T16:36:56-08:00","id":1183758,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"309\" data-vbnamecard=\"309\">White Oak Dragon</a><br /> <br /> Thanks; if your kith gets taken in for an official one, I may change the name to Soul Shooter, as the Trickery implies a Changeling uses part of herself for her weapon. Best of luck. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7920_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7920\" data-vbnamecard=\"7920\">Master Aquatosic</a> <br /> <br /> Hmmm, when using Firearms to shoot a moving target is an interesting idea, or possibly for shooting a distant one. I had thought that perhaps when a Deadeye uses the Aim option, since that is a risk/reward scenario, but I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> As for the Trickery, it's more to allow a Changeling both to leave a calling card and options for actually using a firearm. Note that I mentioned that the gun didn't need to have a magazine in it, which was meant to go across all guns - this means a Changeling can simply carry an empty pistol, spend a glamour and have a full weapon at their disposal, or even simply pick up an empty rifle an opponent was using and use that as if it were fresh. This is partially to work around various places not allowing loaded weaponry on the premises. While having a weapon at all would probably raise brows, one not even having the capacity to carry ammunition would grant the Changeling some leeway. Add in the fact that the ammunition they create is unique to them, and at the end of the scene there is no evidence they were personally carrying it, and you have some interesting scenarios for a hitman.<br /> <br /> My initial idea for the Trickery was that the number of bullets a Changeling got was determined on the successes and half their Wyrd, and that it could exceed storage that way. However, I realized that would be pretty lackluster and random if the Changeling got a low die roll, or overpowered if they had something like a shotgun, so I changed it to simply having the normal maximum storage. I had pondered on another idea where it was Glamour and a die roll to simply make a ranged attack, but that felt a little wasteful to me in terms of glamour, so I decided to simply have it affect a normal gun.<br /> <br /> I suppose there could be another aspect added to it, such as not suffering penalties to Firearms rolls from environmental factors when using their Trickery, or maybe choosing to not cause damage to a target even if successful. After all, Gristlegrinders don't require making a Grappling roll to make bites that have Lethal damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T17:30:53-08:00","id":1183773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1183758#post1183758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span><br /> <br /> Thanks; if your kith gets taken in for an official one, I may change the name to Soul Shooter, as the Trickery implies a Changeling uses part of herself for her weapon. Best of luck. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I suppose there could be another aspect added to it, such as not suffering penalties to Firearms rolls from environmental factors when using their Trickery, or maybe choosing to not cause damage to a target even if successful. After all, Gristlegrinders don't require making a Grappling roll to make bites that have Lethal damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. I've got my fingers crossed. <br /> <br /> One thing that occurred to me was that you could always have the Trickery summon a fully loaded gun mechanically identical to the last firearm they touched that vanishes at the end of the scene or whenever it runs out of ammunition. That would get around the raised eyebrows for carrying an unloaded weapon everywhere they go. If the fired bullets vanished as well, you'd lose the calling card, but add to the weirdness when there is obvious bullet damage without any sign of said bullets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T18:37:39-08:00","id":1183786,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"309\" data-vbnamecard=\"309\">White Oak Dragon</a> <br /> <br /> Hmm, it's an idea, but by that point you're encroaching on what Discreet Summons can do with an easier die roll. Granted, we could make it a bit more flexible and make it any gun that they've touched in the last 24 hours along with the unique ammunition. Heck, the gun could itself be stylized to fit in with their mien to those who can see past it, making it clear that the weapon isn't normal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T12:50:22-08:00","id":1184849,"title":"","content":"Hey, I actually worked on something for the Gameplayer Kith that I thought I'd share. I would appreciate criticism or feedback to help tweak it here and there possibly.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IyWSDrQ8OoEpOxDG8VFPu5Bl_E3TnOPlB7Pp1ytP_0Y/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Gameplayer Kith</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23862-twinsinner","name":"Twinsinner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23862_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T04:57:45-08:00","id":1187262,"title":"","content":"Do a Beast's natural weapons qualify as archaic for Elemental Weapon? (F. e. can a hellhound Changeling &quot;use Fire Fang&quot;?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T10:27:34-08:00","id":1187312,"title":"","content":"I'd say no; they're more akin to natural weapons. Elemental Weapon is for crafted weapons, such as swords, bows and bludgeons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T16:26:36-08:00","id":1188332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1187262#post1187262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do a Beast's natural weapons qualify as archaic for Elemental Weapon? (F. e. can a hellhound Changeling &quot;use Fire Fang&quot;?)</div> </div> </div> </div>You could always house rule that as the contract's seeming benefit for beasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12559-hedgebound-heart","name":"Hedgebound Heart","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T21:51:08-07:00","id":1220437,"title":"","content":"Hey guys, seen a lot of great stuff for Kith Conversions and Homebrew Kiths in here and wanted to get some opinions on one a player and I have been working on. The idea is basically a voice changeling. (<a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/VoiceChangeling\" target=\"_blank\">http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.ph...oiceChangeling</a>)<br /> <br /> Echo (name subject to change, but looking for something that mimics sound perfectly.)<br /> Skill blessing: When using expression to mimic others voices or accents, the Changeling achieves an exceptional success on 3 successes instead of 5<br /> Trickery blessing: Here is where we were having trouble. The player suggested having the above with a glamour cost but without a contested roll, which I really didn't like. Might be possible to do similar to the suggested Chirurgeon blessing in the original post and add Wyrd to mimicry rolls. I feel like that's where I'm headed, but didn't know if anyone else had any ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24249-muattles","name":"Muattles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T23:18:49-07:00","id":1220449,"title":"","content":"Cool idea! I suggest &quot;Lyrebird&quot; as name - they mimic natural and artifical sounds perfectly from other birds to car alarms and chainsaws.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">\u041f\u0438\u0444-\u043f\u0430\u0444 \u043e\u0439-\u043e\u0439-\u043e\u0439 / \u0423\u043c\u0438\u0440\u0430\u0435\u0442 \u0437\u0430\u0439\u0447\u0438\u043a \u043c\u043e\u0439 </span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24224-insane\u2022kismano","name":"Insane\u2022kismanO","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T01:22:01-07:00","id":1220462,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24249-muattles\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24249\" data-vbnamecard=\"24249\">Muattles</a> Funny enough, I had a similar idea for a Kith known as a Beatheart (Heartbeat). The Trickery, which I was tentatively calling &quot;Singing Outside The Box&quot; (Beatboxing) was where they could spend a glamour, roll Presence + Expression, and if they were successful they could perfectly mimic any sound they have heard before. Even if the voice, noise or tone was outside of human range, the Changeling can achieve it, though they may require a specialty in a particular instrument in order to hit all the right notes without a roll.<br /> <br /> The idea was for a Chageling of the Paint Court, who possessed a contract that allows a Changeling to basically make a copy of themselves, and thus with this Kith blessing she could beatbox an entire song by herself. If you want mechanics, I'd recommend looking at the Vox embed from Demon: The Descent (it is in Flowers Of Hell). Just remember, Wyrd rarely factors into 2e Kiths save for if it is inflicting a condition on another person. Hope this helped some.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T04:35:24-07:00","id":1221652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muattles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1220437#post1220437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey guys, seen a lot of great stuff for Kith Conversions and Homebrew Kiths in here and wanted to get some opinions on one a player and I have been working on. The idea is basically a voice changeling. (<a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/VoiceChangeling\" target=\"_blank\">http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.ph...oiceChangeling</a>)<br /> <br /> Echo (name subject to change, but looking for something that mimics sound perfectly.)<br /> Skill blessing: When using expression to mimic others voices or accents, the Changeling achieves an exceptional success on 3 successes instead of 5<br /> Trickery blessing: Here is where we were having trouble. The player suggested having the above with a glamour cost but without a contested roll, which I really didn't like. Might be possible to do similar to the suggested Chirurgeon blessing in the original post and add Wyrd to mimicry rolls. I feel like that's where I'm headed, but didn't know if anyone else had any ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I were to make a kith like this, I would probably make their skill trick work for mimicking any sound they\u2019ve heard previously, rather than only voices. Their Trickery would allow them to spend Glamour to make their voice seem to emanate from any place they wish, provided it is within their line of sight. For the name, I would call them Echosongs. And now I want to write them up. I\u2019m not going to do so (at least not any time soon), as I have other things I need to write, but I do want to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T17:20:19-07:00","id":1222549,"title":"","content":"<b>Brazilian Kiths</b><br /> <br /> <b>Boitat\u00e1</b><br /> Among the Brazilian Changelings, the Boitat\u00e1 is remembered for his powerful presence and passion. Boitat\u00e1 is a giant snake with fiery eyes, they love staying in the water but once they are outside, their body is infused with a blue flame. It is always defending fiercely the forests and woods from hunters. It is said that looking at the Boitat\u00e1 eyes can make you mad and blind. Others sayd that it eats eyes when it is angry. Or that it is the soul of evil people, burning everything in its path.<br /> <b>KIth blessing:</b> Boitat\u00e1 gains half its Wyrd rating for Perception rolls and gains the unseen sense merit.<br /> <br /> <b>Iara</b><br /> Iara is an indigenous woman who lives in the Amazon river, seducing her victims, bringing them to the river, then drowning and devouring them, just like the Greek sirens. The Iara is described as having long green or black hair. Some people say that if a man scapes the Iara's enchantments he will become crazy and only an indigenous shaman (known as Paj\u00e9 in Brazil) will cure him.<br /> <b>KIth blessing:</b> Iara gains its Wyrd rating for a Seduction roll. But after a succesful roll she must gain glamour from her victim or the victim will gain a derangement.<br /> <br /> <b>Curupira</b><br /> The Curupira is a protector of the forests. He uses a wild boar as a mount. He has red hair and his feet is turned backwards. When he walks, his footprints confuses people tracking him since they are pointing to the opposite side. He is very aggressive towards hunters. People say a Curupira can change a hunter into an animal and make it become hunted as some sort of vengeance.Kith <b>Kith Blessing: </b>People tracking you have a penalty equal to your Wyrd in order to pursue or chase you. You also gain an Animal Ken specialisation.<br /> <br /> <b>Saci-Perer\u00ea</b><br /> Often described as a black child wearing a red hood, having only one leg, and always smoking a pipe. It is the Brazilian Pooka, described often as a mischievious. The Saci-Perer\u00ea can turn himself into a whirlwind. He is a free spirit, always joyful and looking for fun. He has holes in his hands.<br /> <b>Kith Blessing: </b>You gain half your Wyrd in rolls to gain glamour if you used treachery to generate emotion.<br /> <br /> <b>Mula-sem-Cabe\u00e7a</b><br /> People say that if a woman seduces a priest, she will become a mula-sem-cabe\u00e7a, a mule without a head. That mule doesn't have a head and fire is spread out of its nostrils even if said nostrils is in a non-existent head.<br /> <b>Kith Blessing: </b>Seduction rolls to gain glamour has the 8 again rule. If you make a succesful roll the victim forgets your appearance and facial features. Damage from fire is reduced by your Wyrd level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24237,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24237-pluvinarch","user":"Pluvinarch","date":". 05-27-2018, 08:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24237-pluvinarch","name":"Pluvinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T17:34:18-07:00","id":1223441,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hello all, could I get thoughts/ suggestions on this kith idea for a game I am running soon?</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Phooka:</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Kith Blessing: When the Phooka uses persuasion to convince someone of a course of action, achieving three successes counts as an exceptional success.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bringer of fair and foul fortunes: Once per scene, the Phooka may spend one glamour and make a wits + subterfuge roll to curse or bless any individual she has a pledge, promise or deal with (add or subtract one die from their next action for each point of the Phooka's Wyrd -to a maximum of +/- 5).</span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13217-ember16","name":"Ember16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T08:59:35-07:00","id":1223641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ember16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1223441#post1223441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hello all, could I get thoughts/ suggestions on this kith idea for a game I am running soon?</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Phooka:</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Kith Blessing: When the Phooka uses persuasion to convince someone of a course of action, achieving three successes counts as an exceptional success.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bringer of fair and foul fortunes: Once per scene, the Phooka may spend one glamour and make a wits + subterfuge roll to curse or bless any individual she has a pledge, promise or deal with (add or subtract one die from their next action for each point of the Phooka's Wyrd -to a maximum of +/- 5).</span><br /> </div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ll need to give some thought to the trickery aspect. The skill trick you\u2019ve given them seems a bit general to me, though. What is the niche you\u2019ve got in mind for them? The description of the kith could help here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T11:58:00-07:00","id":1223680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1223641#post1223641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019ll need to give some thought to the trickery aspect. The skill trick you\u2019ve given them seems a bit general to me, though. What is the niche you\u2019ve got in mind for them? The description of the kith could help here.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, quite honestly, that description could easily fit any use of the Persuasion skill","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T13:20:10-07:00","id":1223697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1223680#post1223680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah, quite honestly, that description could easily fit any use of the Persuasion skill</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yes, you are both right.... how about this: &quot;<span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When the Phooka uses persuasion to offer counsel, achieving three successes counts as an exceptional success.&quot;? I am mostly basing this Kith off of its namesake, 'Phookas' as </span>mischievous<span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (though sometimes helpful) guides and advisers. <br /> <br /> As for the Trickery, right now I feel as though it s A) possibly overpowered and B) not terribly unique. Any thoughts/ suggestions to help with that would be much appreciated.</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13217-ember16","name":"Ember16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T11:16:20-07:00","id":1223964,"title":"","content":"<b>Modern Kiths</b><br /> <br /> True Fae are always being influenced by human culture. From myths to folklore to fairy tales. Nowadays comic books, movies, series, animations and videogames are carrying the storetelling sources of ancient times. But stories are also spreading through urban legends and internet myths...<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Slenderman:</b> You have been turned into a faceless pale creature with elongated arms wearing a suit. Now you stalk the forests and spread fear in order to make teenagers avoid your Keeper hunting ground.<br /> <b>Kith Blessing:</b> You can make a grapple attack from a distance of Wyrd yards from your victim. A grappled victim can also give you a bonus glamour equal to half your Wyrd value. You can't attack people who are carrying at least 10 sheets of paper.<br /> <br /> <b>Bloody Mary:</b> A monster who can be summoned by unwary people. Repeat your name three times in front of a mirror in the dark and you will come. You did this once and your Keeper came for you. Now you are back to the right side of the mirror trying to maintain your clarity, but you look like an undead woman filled with blood and shards of glass.<br /> <b>Kith Blessing:</b> Giving your true name to someone make you summonable by then. All they need is to cry your name three times in front of a mirror in a dark place. You feel a calling force permeating you from the moment the first time your name is ushered in this condition. At the third time you are immediately transported to your summoner. You are also compelled to take glamour from your caller (or you can try to resist a Will roll) and you gain bonus glamour equal to your Wyrd if you make a succesful glamour roll. Many Bloody Marys try to make their True Name infamous on creepy internet circles in order to gain a consistent source of glamour.<br /> <br /> <b>Creepypasta:</b> You played the wrong videogame. Your Keeper jumped from your gameboy screen and captured you. Slaved in a mad parody of a Pokemon world, you did his bidding until a glitch gave you a mean to scape his realm. Now you stalk videogames in order to scare unwary teenagers.<br /> <b>Kith Blessing:</b> You can step into a videogame in order to haunt its player. You enter a videogame from your dreams, making a Computer + Wyrd roll to find gateways from your dream to a videogame being played at the moment. Once on the desired videogame setting you can subtly change it by using dreamscaping methods. The experience the player has from that game will generate glamour for you, with a bonus equal to your Wyrd. Very scary experiences can be a breaking point for the player.<br /> <b>Alternate kith: Deepweb.</b> The Deepweb has the same scaring method of the creepypasta but it attacks people using deepweb navigators instead of videogame players.<br /> <br /> <b>Trollface:</b> You were captured by a troll. A digital one. He was a bully, the biggest one you have ever seen. He hurt you emotionally by being the insensible jerk it is. You eventually became a monster just like him, a human with a large pale face with a mockery of a grin, trollface.<br /> <b>Kith Blessing:</b> You can gain glamour by posting on internet forums and social medias. You must roll Manipulation + Empathy + Wyrd. On a Success, you also gain bonus glamour equal to your Wyrd. You can only do this once per game session. On a dramatic failure you are banned from the forum/site you used. You can't have access even if you create a new fake avatar.<br /> <b>Alternate kith:</b> <b>Faker. </b>You gain glamour on social medias but by spreading fake news.<br /> <b>Alternate kith:</b> <b>Memer. </b>You gain glamour on social medias but by spreading memes. You also look like a meme, most probably a cat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24237-pluvinarch","name":"Pluvinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T11:33:15-07:00","id":1223967,"title":"","content":"These are 1e Kiths. This thread is for the more powerful 2e kiths, which are standardized like this.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Skill Trick</u></b>: a way of using a certain Skill or Skills which the character is supernaturally good at, giving them an exceptional success on three successes instead of five.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Trickery</u></b>: an overtly supernatural trick that costs a single Glamour per use. Should relate to the same overall concept, but generally not provide an advantage for the same action the skill trick covers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 06-01-2018, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T01:56:15-07:00","id":1237438,"title":"","content":"Here's a custom Kith I cooked up earlier tonight.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Pixel</b></u><br /> <i>I still can\u2019t get over how weird it is to be using electronics that aren\u2019t me. Mind, that\u2019s easy enough to fix.</i><br /> <br /> The Gentry aren't known for their love of modern electronics, but not all Keepers are behind the times. Many find the digital age fascinating, enough that they wish to have their own versions at hand. Sometimes a Token will suffice, but most find that the cost is too tedious for the benefits the hardware grants. The Gentry thus find that the best way to get the true digital experience is to find someone who has experienced it themselves. Pixels are the end result, serving as either the hardware for the Gentry to enjoy their online fun, or the living software for electronics that a Keeper happens to take a fancy to. More than one programmer, repairmen and or those who spend more than an hour a day on their machines have found themselves as the new Clippit offering suggestions for what their Keeper would want to view.<br /> <br /> Life as a Pixel is a hard one. Even without their masters dictating what they must do, the flow of information that runs through or past a Pixel often acts like a sedative, facts, figures and fictions buzzing too fast for them to keep a hold of who they are. Sometimes such data is simply torture for them to sift through, only the looming threat of destruction keeping them going fast enough to stay ahead of the requests. Even if they don't slip up or make an off comment, however, the Gentry are fickle and may scrap or delete a Pixel for only doing what they are supposed to do, and not what their Keeper wants them to do. Others are just forgotten, turned off and left in some dusty corner of a manor filled with other trinkets and baubles to experiment with.<br /> <br /> Whatever their use, it is in the downtime that a Pixel often finds the time to simply disconnect themselves from their work. A Pixel that serves as a desktop may literally unplug themselves from the wall and lumber off, whereas another who served as a web browser could find herself longing for the places on the screen and remember they once actually went there before stepping past the monitor. A lack of data, a line of similar requests allowing for multitasking or even simple commands taken too literally can lead to a Pixel trying to escape their Keeper's realm. Not all make it. Those who do often find themselves fitting right back into the world of facebook and pizza Ironside has become.<br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> All of her features are slightly granulated, and her eyes are back-lit screens that go black when she sleeps. She is also an avid programmer, and the first on the scene to ascertain the Freehold's digital security.<br /> <b>Wizened:</b> He is the Freehold's best hacker, and is often found wrapped up in his work. His hair is wire, his eyes are cracked cameras, and his fingers click with every move they make, but when push comes to shove he is the best at his job.<br /> <br /> <b>Kith Blessing:</b> Whenever a Pixel uses Computers to hack into or create a program, they achieve an Exceptional Success on three successes.<br /> <br /> <i>Patched In:</i> By spending a point of Glamour and succeeding a Presence + Computers roll, a Pixel may touch and patch themselves into a piece of computer hardware, be it a smartphone, an aging library desktop or even something as simple as an electronic safe door. So long as it has a computer chip in it and an interface they can utilize, a Pixel can patch themselves into it. Once they have done so, they are integrated into the system, allowing them to move the hardware as it if were their own body and reflexively access any documents or files as though they were the owner/admin of the machine. Passwords and firewalls may still stand between them and what they wish to access, but any Hacking rolls for a Pixel happen reflexively and with the hardware's own equipment bonus benefiting them, practically at the speed of thought.<br /> <br /> While Patched In is active the Changeling is physically attached to the hardware they are accessing, which may or may not impede movement. They can detach themselves reflexively at any time, or be forcibly removed. Forceful disconnecting requires a successful Strength + Brawl roll with successes exceeding those of the activation roll for Patched In; doing so deals a point of Lethal damage to the Pixel and, if fragile enough, could damage the hardware as well. A Pixel may also be counter-hacked if someone else infiltrates the hardware they are using, though the Pixel may fight back using the hardware's equipment bonus as their own. If the hacker succeeds, Patched In ends and the Pixel takes two Bashing damage.<br /> <br /> <br /> Let me know what you guys think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":".  Added the Kith quote 07-31-2018, 02:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T07:30:47-07:00","id":1237496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1237438#post1237438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a custom Kith I cooked up earlier tonight.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Pixel</b></u><br /> <br /> ...<br /> Let me know what you guys think.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like what you\u2019ve come up with here. Their blessing reminds me a bit of the Cybersage (one of my Underhill kiths). I really like how broad you made their potential roles in Arcadia, while still maintaining consistency in how it affected them. Very well done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T17:28:39-07:00","id":1238726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1237496#post1237496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like what you\u2019ve come up with here. Their blessing reminds me a bit of the Cybersage (one of my Underhill kiths). I really like how broad you made their potential roles in Arcadia, while still maintaining consistency in how it affected them. Very well done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the feedback; honestly, the Kith was inspired by a discord discussion where someone noted their friend's literal Computer Mouse character. I thought on it a bit, and the name Pixels was very close to Pixies...and I just ran with it. Really happy with what came out. I've got more Kiths I need to finish up, but hopefully they'll come out as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T03:38:16-07:00","id":1239620,"title":"","content":"Anyone have any ideas for the Trickery part of Riddleseeker's Blessing? The Skill part is easy enough, Exceptional Success on 3 Dice for Investigation when dealing with Riddles, but I can't think of a good Trickery Blessing for them x.x<br /> <br /> I honestly don't want to try and slip away with just adding to the pool of all Wits rolls like in 1E, and the previous 2E iteration of just giving them an additional point of Wits is obviously not in line with Trickery.... So yeah, a bit at a loss on direction.<br /> <br /> Riddleseekers are all about Cunning and Curiosity, and that's what I Love about the kith..... Maybe something about Research or Learning new bits of information, Puzzles? I'm just out of it right now (Should honestly be asleep right now X3) but I thought I'd ask....<br /> <br /> Thank you in advance for any ideas, suggestions, or advice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/24296274/BeastThePrimordial.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":6566,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","user":"Draca","date":". 07-28-2018, 06:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","name":"Draca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6566_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T04:14:40-07:00","id":1239623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draca</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1239620#post1239620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone have any ideas for the Trickery part of Riddleseeker's Blessing? The Skill part is easy enough, Exceptional Success on 3 Dice for Investigation when dealing with Riddles, but I can't think of a good Trickery Blessing for them x.x<br /> <br /> I honestly don't want to try and slip away with just adding to the pool of all Wits rolls like in 1E, and the previous 2E iteration of just giving them an additional point of Wits is obviously not in line with Trickery.... So yeah, a bit at a loss on direction.<br /> <br /> Riddleseekers are all about Cunning and Curiosity, and that's what I Love about the kith..... Maybe something about Research or Learning new bits of information, Puzzles? I'm just out of it right now (Should honestly be asleep right now X3) but I thought I'd ask....<br /> <br /> Thank you in advance for any ideas, suggestions, or advice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would spending a point of Glamour to bind a listener to Sealing to answer a Riddle the Riddleseeker knows work? Like the Sphinx. Or is involuntary Sealing too against concept? Maybe invert it - they can Gain a point of Glamour by solving new Riddles?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T06:09:17-07:00","id":1239649,"title":"","content":"What about making it so that any time someone tries mundanely to place a Condition on them (specifically a socially based one like Leveraged or Swooning), the Riddleseeker can spend a point of Glamour to challenge them to a riddle contest. If the Riddleseeker wins, the Condition settles on their opponent instead, but if they lose their opponent must reveal the answer to the riddle. You could call it Riddles in the Dark, and what one has in their pockets would be totally fair game. That\u2019s just a rough idea, of course, but I think leveraging their riddles in some way to gain power over someone or squeeze information from them is the angle you\u2019d want. Just don\u2019t make the roll require the same Skill as their skill trick.<br /> Alternatively, you could give them the ability to reveal information in a manner that people don\u2019t understand, disguising it through the Subterfuge Skill. Basically, if someone applied Leveraged or something similar and demanded your password to resolve it, you could offer it in riddle form to resolve the Condition. They\u2019d need to solve the riddle to gain the information.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","user":"White Oak Dragon","date":". 07-28-2018, 09:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T10:28:42-07:00","id":1239727,"title":"","content":"Love the ideas guys, thank you very, much! I think Ill go with either White Oak's first suggestion, or a combination of White Oak's and Vent0's second suggestions.....<br /> <br /> For the first one I think the roll should be either Wits + Academics, or Manipulation + Subterfuge or maybe just Wits + Subterfuge......... Know what I really like that third option, it makes Riddleseeker's want Wits(their whole thing in previous iterations), and Subterfuge really works for what the effect is going for..... I think I'm gonna go with Riddles in the Dark.... Thank you again White Oak, and Vent0.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/24296274/BeastThePrimordial.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","name":"Draca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6566_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T12:44:17-07:00","id":1239766,"title":"","content":"No problem. Glad I could help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T17:42:40-07:00","id":1239853,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6566_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6566\" data-vbnamecard=\"6566\">Draca</a> maybe:<br /> <br /> Spend a point of Glamour and roll Wits+Investigation+Wyrd, target must use its action each turn to roll an extended Intelligence+Investigation(riddles) until they achieve a number of successes equal to the activation roll. If they fail then the Changeling either opens a Door (Social Manuevering) or inflicts the Insensate tilt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T00:45:14-07:00","id":1239926,"title":"","content":"hmmms how about this Riddles in the Dark: When someone tries to mundanely place a Social Condition (like Leveraged or Swooning) on the Riddleseeker, she can spend a point of Glamour and roll Wits+Subterfuge in order to reverse the situation. The target may resist with a roll of Intelligence+Investigation(riddles). If the target fails then the changeling may open a Door(Social Maneuvering), the target gains the Confused condition, or the target gains the Insensate tilt. If the target succeeds in resisting, the Riddleseeker may reveal any information probed for in a manner the target may not understand, disguising it as a riddle to resolve the condition.<br /> <br /> How does this sound? Is it too much? <br /> <br /> btw, what does Sealing do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/24296274/BeastThePrimordial.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":6566,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","user":"Draca","date":". 07-30-2018, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","name":"Draca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6566_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T20:22:59-07:00","id":1247596,"title":"","content":"<br /> Mannikin<br /> <i>I\u2019ll do it for sure\u2026But </i>how<i> do you want it done? </i><br /> <br /> The Gentry wanted something from you. And it decided the only way that was going to happen was if you could bend and flex to their design.<br /> <br /> They made you into a doll with soft plastic features and interchangeable outfits. Or maybe they made you into the archetypal dummy or stringed puppet straight out of Pinocchio. Whichever it is, you were remade into something that could be positioned to any role your Keeper saw fit. You were their toy.<br /> <br /> But not anymore. Your joints still have the ball bearings placed there so long ago but now you choose how they move and you choose what role you play.<br /> <br /> <i>Wizened: </i>You were made to fill a role and expected to excel at it. Time and time again you tried to fit the model given to you but was never enough and still you\u2019re a perfectionist in whatever roll you\u2019re to play.<br /> <i>Elemental: </i>You were made, remade, posed, reposed, discarded, painted, and encased. Always changing and always moving. But like a winding river, this same momentum of change was also your ticket to freedom. You freed yourself, inch by inch and pose by pose but eventually you freed yourself. You\u2019ve been changing your entire durance and it earned your freedom, why stop now?<br /> <br /> <b>Kith Blessing: </b>When a Mannikin uses Expression at another\u2019s behest or benefit, achieving three successes counts as an exceptional success.<br /> <br /> <i>Role Player: </i>A Manikin is adept at posing and fitting in as different roles, even ones that are someone new to them. They can spend a point of Glamour to imitate and single action or role by rolling Dexterity + Subterfuge + Wyrd. The pretend action is just that, pretend and does not actually do anything other than fool on-lookers. However, if an exceptional success is made, a +2 bonus is conferred if the Manikin chooses to attempt the action for real.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":654,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","user":"xiongrey","date":". 08-18-2018, 11:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-30T17:15:26-07:00","id":1258298,"title":"","content":"Hey this is my first Kith, i don't know if someone already did a version of Flamesiren but i did one because my sister's character is a Flamesiren<br /> <br /> <u><b>Flamesiren</b></u><br /> <i>Oh dear, better keep those hands for yourself, trust me, would be a really mess explain to your husband what happened to you.</i><br /> <br /> The living embodiment of the seductive flame, the dancing and sparkling flame of a bonfire in the darkness, in fact some consider Flamesirens the absolute &quot;look but don't touch&quot; specially those who got in ther bad side.<br /> Most Flamesiren were full of <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">unfulfilled</span> desires and aspirations, maybe in the Flamesiren previous life he could never become the famous journalist he wanted to be or maybe her was confined in a job as a high school teacher while dreaming of being great researchers but True Fae are also specially interested in frustrated dancers from the big dancer who was getting too old for to keep dancing or maybe the dancer who never had his skill recognized<br /> <br /> Your skin was transformed in your frustrated passion, flaming and seducing but never touchable, with time you learned how to use this on your behalf, how to control your flames and how to use your skills to find an exit of the nightmare they put you in<br /> <br /> <b>Beast: </b>The flaming bird dances a savage and unique dance while her feathers spread in the air in the middle of the stage glimmering like if they were sparks of a bird-like bonfire<br /> <br /> <b>Darkling: </b>Compose by dark and blue flames the dark ballerina dances an enigmatic and enticing dance that is capable of making anyone be the moths of her dark flame<br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> A slightly translucent glimmering skin, hair made of fire, eyes like dancing flames and the most rebellious and awesome dance you saw in your life<br /> <br /> <b>Elemental: </b>His body is made of pure fire and his dance is the most passionate and intense than anything you saw in your life even capable of inflaming your most ardent passions<br /> <br /> <b>Kith Blessing: </b>When doing an expression check for a performance for a crowd she need just 3 dices instead of 5 for an exceptional success.<br /> <i>The Touch of the Dancing Flame: </i>Any time your character succeeds in a performance, you may spend points of glamour to<br /> inflict the swooning condition, the amount of people inflicted is based on how many points of glamour were expended(can't be more than 5)<br /> Anyone with the Swooning Condition who touches the flamesiren treats him as an Fire with the size of a bonfire with level equal to half the flamesiren\u2019s Wyrd, rounded down(Can't be more than Level 3 bunsen Burner).<br /> <br /> Edited: Sorry for the extreme delay in fixing it, i still think gonna need some balancing on the &quot;<i>The Touch of the Dancing Flame&quot; </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24396,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24396-queer-snake","user":"Queer Snake","date":". 10-23-2018, 08:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24396-queer-snake","name":"Queer Snake","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-03T07:58:10-07:00","id":1258735,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24396-queer-snake\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24396\" data-vbnamecard=\"24396\">Queer Snake</a> I think that looks pretty good, though don't Extreme Environments take a while to take effect? Maybe something could be done with the rules for fire?<br /> <br /> I had an idea for a kith conversion yesterday. It's somewhat straightforward while also attempting to maintain the metaphorical aspects.<br /> <br /> <b>Broadback</b><br /> <br /> <i>Tired already? Can't say I'm ready to quit just yet. Hop on, I'll give you a ride.</i><br /> <br /> Some Gentry are attracted to tenacity and stubbornness. Perhaps they see a bit of themselves in such traits, or maybe they just want a challenge to break. Other Fae just need a pack mule or minotaur, and the other aspects come later. Regardless, Broadbacks are changelings with the traits of goats, oxen, donkeys, horses, and other hoofed beasts of burden, coupled with a strong will and enduring constitution.<br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> This goat-legged satyr is always ready to party. He even has this trick for opening bottles of beer on his horns. You should check it out.<br /> <br /> <b>Ogre:</b> Even under the Mask, people would describe them as &quot;built like an ox.&quot; Sure, with their broad, looming frame and long ivory horns, their more than a little bit of a bull in a china shop, but that's never slowed them down before, and won't now either.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> When making an Athletics roll to cross rough terrain, an Exceptional Success is achieved with three successes instead of five.<br /> <br /> <i>Stoic Forbearance:</i> Choose a Resistance Attribute. When the Broadback makes a roll other than Perception that uses the chosen Attribute, they may spend a point of Glamour to add their Wyrd (to a maximum of +5) to the dice pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-04T13:07:54-07:00","id":1258936,"title":"","content":"Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1423_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1423\" data-vbnamecard=\"1423\">espritdecalmar</a> and yes the rules for fire work much better than Extreme Enviroment, i will define the size and heat of the fire","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24396-queer-snake","name":"Queer Snake","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T06:59:54-07:00","id":1300541,"title":"","content":"Something I literally <u>just</u> finished:<br /> <br /> <u><b>Fireheart</b></u><br /> <i> As the flames charred my flesh, their light burned its way into my mind. It\u2019s still there, you know, dancing behind my eyes in the back of my brain. Do not try to hide anything from me; I will find it every time.</i><br /> Even within their own demesnes, the Others still have need of fire. One True Fae might require a glorious chandelier to light a ballroom, while another needs its heat to warm their parlor. Still another might need to burn away a grove of withered Thorns to clear space into which they may expand their holdings. Such endeavors are costly, and rather than simply invoke Contracts or influences (which might be outside their purviews), many Gentry will invest that Glamour to create a Fireheart.<br /> Mortals chosen for this Kith are invariably curious. Their eyes and minds are always open to new experiences or knowledge, and they will go out of their way to find them \u2013 sometimes endangering themselves to do so. These people are easy marks for even a remotely competent privateer, so the True Fae rarely need to involve themselves directly in the hunt, save for the manufacture of the fetch. Too often, such a mortal simply walks into their own abduction by the nose of their own inquisitive nature.<br /> The durance of a Fireheart invariably begins in pain, as their Keeper literally burns Glamour into their flesh to effect the change. The pain ebbs, of course, but the burning never stops. Once back in the real world, these Lost usually turn their Fae-keen eyes and ears toward investigative work. Many become detectives or spies for their chosen Court. Some align themselves directly to their Freehold, using their talents to root out privateers and other threats.<br /> <i> Darkling:</i> Pale blue or green flames dance behind the character\u2019s eyes. Similar flames lick across their skin like animated tattoos.<br /> <i>Ogre:</i> Wisps of smoke trickle from between the character\u2019s teeth and constantly waft around their wrists. When angered, a red-gold fire ignites in their mouth and around their fists.<br /> <i>Wizened:</i> The character\u2019s eyes resemble lumps of burnt-down charcoal \u2013 white and gray with the dim red glow of cooling embers.<br /> <b> Kith Blessing:</b> When a Fireheart uses Investigation to locate something that is hidden or concealed, achieving three successes counts as an exceptional success.<br /> <i>Flickering Acumen:</i> A Fireheart\u2019s senses are unusually keen and in constant motion, allowing them to predict movements and react accordingly. A Fireheart may spend 1 point of Glamour to add half of their Wyrd rating (minimum of 1) to either Wits-based dice pools or both Initiative and Defense for the remainder of the scene. The changeling retains the Defense bonus that this Blessing provides in any situation where they would normally lose their Defense.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5766-nouveaurich","name":"NouveauRich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5766_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T20:43:38-07:00","id":1303877,"title":"","content":"A while ago I attempted to convert the Lurkglider Kith from Winter Masques 1st Edition to 2nd Edition and I was wondering if you all would be willing to give me some feedback, I basically used it as it was written for the most part. I would also welcome any suggestions on the examples of how this Kith would be adapted to various Seemings. The character I used it for was an Ogre. <br /> <br /> The Lurkglider achieves an exceptional Success with 3 Successes when using athletics to maintain balance on small footholds<br /> Gargoyle\u2019s Grace: By spending a point of Glamour and making a Dexterity + Athletics roll the Lurkglider may dive from up to 100 yards without taking damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24961-darklander","name":"Darklander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T10:48:39-08:00","id":1346207,"title":"","content":"Reviving this thread with a new kith. I like my own fluff for it but am still workshopping the seeming descriptions and the mechanical bits<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Hecatoncheir</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>No, I don't need a spotter. Trust me, all hands are on deck here.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">They say many hands make short work, but that means little when the boss never stops giving you work. Just as on Earth, sometimes you find impoverished Gentry. As powerful as they are to their human and hob victims, they are a mid-sized fish in a sea full of sharks. Sharks who find it diverting and healthy to mess with them, raid their lands and poach their best slaves. So these &quot;minor&quot; gentry need to make the most use out of whatever slaves they could keep around and hide. Thus, one changeling is built to do the work of an entire team of servants.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Those who survive without dying from exhaustion are often those who were already used to this life. Perhaps she was the overworked homemaker who had to balance all the needs of a toddler, a teenager, a college student and an immature husband. Maybe he was a janitor at a run-down school, acting as clean-up crew, electrician, heating technician or whoever else the school didn't have the money to hire. Or maybe they were a multimedia artist, painting landscapes over the abstract surfaces of their own free-form sculptures.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When they escape, they often do so by using that same adaptability to overcome the obstacles put in their. Sometimes they break free in a whirling dervish of chaos, smashing through a wall with a sledgehammer before swapping to a shield to block the dragon\u2019s fire. Sometimes, they just realize one day that they have taken up every function in the entire realm, leaving no other servants or guards to stop them from just running off.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Elemental:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> She is a swirling mass of mud that defaults to a vaguely humanoid shape, but when pressed, she shapes out new appendages as needed.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Darkling:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> compound eyes dart around as he uses one set of arms to navigate the book while another transcribes it simultaneously</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Blessing</b>:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> when using Dexterity to perform an extended action, three successes count as an exceptional success.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Multitasker</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: By spending 1 glamour and passing a Wits + Wyrd roll, a Hecatonchier can hold Wyrd/2 (rounded up) different two-item sets of (physically present and hand-held) equipment or weapons in reserve for the rest of the scene. They can swap out which set is active with an unrolled reflexive action, exchanging one set of benefits for another.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 11-05-2019, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T10:52:26-08:00","id":1346210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darklander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1303877#post1303877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A while ago I attempted to convert the Lurkglider Kith from Winter Masques 1st Edition to 2nd Edition and I was wondering if you all would be willing to give me some feedback, I basically used it as it was written for the most part. I would also welcome any suggestions on the examples of how this Kith would be adapted to various Seemings. The character I used it for was an Ogre.<br /> <br /> The Lurkglider achieves an exceptional Success with 3 Successes when using athletics to maintain balance on small footholds<br /> Gargoyle\u2019s Grace: By spending a point of Glamour and making a Dexterity + Athletics roll the Lurkglider may dive from up to 100 yards without taking damage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Seems good to me. can't think of anything to change","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T12:28:25-08:00","id":1346241,"title":"","content":"Since it's revived, here's a conversion that I came up with a while back:<br /> <br /> <b>Woodwalker</b><br /> <i>Lost? Can't say the term's ever been my cup of tea.</i><br /> <br /> Arcadia is land of sweeping, majestic beauty; it is also a realm of hidden dangers lurking in trees, caves, and mires. The landscape shifts according the whims of its Fae owner, or based on a set of Byzantine, arcane rules. Sometimes not even the Gentry can manage to keep up, or they'd rather just have one of their changeling captives take care of guiding the others through blasted wastelands or windswept deserts. That's where the Woodwalkers come in.<br /> <br /> Most changelings who wind up as members of this kith were already intimately familiar with wilderness environments. They may have been forest rangers, deep-sea fishers, hermits, or members of a nomadic tribe. Others still come from those who romanticized natural and wild places, such as a land-locked soul who longed for a life at sea, or an office worker in the big city who saved up both vacation and sick leave for a long sojourn in the canyons.<br /> <br /> Despite the name, there are Woodwalkers connected to every type of environment imaginable. Any place where a traveler risks getting lost is a place to which members of this kith might attune themselves. There are Woodwalkers of steaming jungles, river deltas, deep grottoes, and even a few who master labyrinthine urban environments, weaving through glass, concrete, and neighborhood watches with ease.<br /> <br /> Escape more often than not comes from outmaneuvering the Gentry in their own environs, learning the land better and more intimately than its master ever would dare. Some find their ways to other domains with radically different landscapes, where interlopers lacking the Woodwalker's gift are at a steep disadvantage. Some even find that by treating the trees and brooks with kindness causes these features to return the favor, guiding changelings along hidden paths back to the Hedge and beyond.<br /> <br /> <i>Elemental:</i> A creature of snow and lichen who sometimes acts as though the tundra where they make their home is an extension of their own being. Trespassers in their domain take their lives into their own hands.<br /> <br /> <i>Wizened:</i> A stooped figure with a gnarled walking stick and roughspun cloak. They know every nook and cranny of this holler, and they'll get you where you need to go, so long as you follow close behind and don't ask too many questions.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Choose a general type of environment (such as forests, islands, plains, mountains, or swamps); when making Survival rolls in the chosen environment, three successes counts as an exceptional success.<br /> <br /> <i>Lay of the Land:</i> While within their environment of expertise, the Woodwalker can spend a point of Glamour as an instant action and roll Wits + Survival. Each success allows the changeling the ask the Storyteller one question from the list below:<ul><li>What is the safest path forward?</li> <li>Where is the nearest source of danger?</li> <li>What is something hidden here?</li> <li>What here is unnatural for the environment?</li> <li>What is something that has changed since the last time I have been here?</li> </ul>Answers received pertain to anything within (Wyrd x 10) yards/meters of the changeling. The Storyteller must answer the player honestly, but does not have to provide context. Successes can be allocated to the same question multiple times for additional information of the same type.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1423,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","user":"espritdecalmar","date":". 11-05-2019, 04:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T13:04:41-08:00","id":1346247,"title":"","content":"nice, but a maximum of 10 meters seems too low. These guys are masters of their domain. I'd give them at least a Wyrd X 10 meter detection radius and maybe even give them a detection radius of [Wyrd] miles","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T13:37:17-08:00","id":1346262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1346247#post1346247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">nice, but a maximum of 10 meters seems too low. These guys are masters of their domain. I'd give them at least a Wyrd X 10 meter detection radius and maybe even give them a detection radius of [Wyrd] miles</div> </div> </div> </div>Good catch with that. Readjusting now. . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T12:02:40-08:00","id":1346807,"title":"","content":"I'm really still not happy with my Hecatoncheir Kith. Can I get some help figuring out how to make their mechanics better fit their description?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T18:34:23-08:00","id":1347153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1346807#post1346807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really still not happy with my Hecatoncheir Kith. Can I get some help figuring out how to make their mechanics better fit their description?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not a system expert or anything, but would it make sense if, for each success on their Wyrd + Wits roll, they were able to hold one additional hand's worth of objects? This would not grant any additional actions, but it would allow them to gain any passive bonuses from all of the objects and to use any of them without needing to take an action to drop and draw. The &quot;exceptional success&quot; blessing also seems a little broad-- might it be better to say any extended dexterity roll using their hands or arms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12108-gscrap","name":"gscrap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12108_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T04:03:03-08:00","id":1347439,"title":"","content":"Does anyone happen to have any ideas for a 2e version of the Nix? The best I can come up with is a re-skinned version of Artist, but using vocal Specialties for Persuasion and Expression, and having the skill bonus apply to Athletics rolls made to swim. Is there a better way that isn't just a copy-paste of another kin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T08:17:39-08:00","id":1347474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1347439#post1347439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone happen to have any ideas for a 2e version of the Nix? The best I can come up with is a re-skinned version of Artist, but using vocal Specialties for Persuasion and Expression, and having the skill bonus apply to Athletics rolls made to swim. Is there a better way that isn't just a copy-paste of another kin?</div> </div> </div> </div>You could have their Blessing apply to Persuasion rolls while in a body of water. For their Trickery. . . that's trickier. Although you'd like to avoid copy-pasting, the Nightsinger kith might have what you're looking for. What is the purpose of the Nix? Fleshing out why the Gentry would turn someone into this kith, or the types of people suited for it, might usher inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T10:51:11-08:00","id":1347506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1347439#post1347439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone happen to have any ideas for a 2e version of the Nix? The best I can come up with is a re-skinned version of Artist, but using vocal Specialties for Persuasion and Expression, and having the skill bonus apply to Athletics rolls made to swim. Is there a better way that isn't just a copy-paste of another kin?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't remember exactly what mechanics the Nix used, but if it could be any aquatic changeling, I'll offer this update to the Swimmerskin/Waterborn/Waterdweller kiths that I posted in this thread a couple years ago:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gscrap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1167923#post1167923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Swimmerskin</b><br /> <br /> <i>Oh yeah? Why don't you jump in here and say that?</i><br /> <br /> The sea is many things: beautiful, mysterious, dangerous, unfathomably vast. It should come as no surprise that many of the Gentry feel an attraction to the water. Changelings with the Swimmerskin kith may have served their durances as pearl divers on the sea floor of a Fae sea, as the creatures that lurk below the waves, or as the waves themselves.<br /> <br /> A majority of Swimmerskins are at their most comfortable in the water, but many tend to avoid the depths except in case of dire emergency.<br /> <br /> Beast: He might almost be attractive, with his lean body and scintillating green scales, but his webbed fingers and faint fishy smell have made it hard to find romance in the freehold. Not for lack of trying, though.<br /> <br /> Elemental: She constantly looks like she just stepped out of a rainstorm, her hair bedraggled and her soaked clothes leaving wet footprints in her wake. When she smiles, which is rarely, her teeth are tiny chips of beach glass.<br /> <br /> Kith Blessing: When the Swimmerskin uses Athletics to swim, achieving three successes counts as an exceptional success.<br /> <br /> <i>Born to the Water</i>: A Swimmerskin is capable of remaining underwater for far longer than an average mortal. When submerged in water, the Swimmerskin can hold her breath for thirty minutes before making any rolls to avoid drowning. Furthermore, she can spend one Glamour to remain submerged indefinitely; however, this effect ends as soon as her head breaks the surface.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm also working on an update to the Palewraith for one of the PCs in a game I'm about to run. I'll skip the fluff for the moment and just ask (humbly) for feedback on the mechanics-- if folks are digging it, I'll post a proper version later on.<br /> <br /> When the Palewraith attempts to navigate or to locate something in total darkness (or otherwise without the benefit of sight), achieving three successes on the roll counts as an exceptional success. A Palewraith may spend one Glamour to add +1 to their Defense rating against physical attacks for one scene. This benefit only applies against attacks made by opponents suffering at least a -1 penalty to vision-related rolls due to darkness or other impairment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12108-gscrap","name":"gscrap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12108_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T11:25:48-08:00","id":1347517,"title":"","content":"Do I repost my update of my Hecatoncheir Kith, or do I just edit it.? What's the server etiquette here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T17:38:41-08:00","id":1347578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1165631-2e-kith-conversion-homebrew?p=1347474#post1347474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You could have their Blessing apply to Persuasion rolls while in a body of water. For their Trickery. . . that's trickier. Although you'd like to avoid copy-pasting, the Nightsinger kith might have what you're looking for. What is the purpose of the Nix? Fleshing out why the Gentry would turn someone into this kith, or the types of people suited for it, might usher inspiration.</div> </div> </div> </div>From original mythology, Nix would use their hypnotic voices to lure people into the water to drown them. In Changeling I could see the Gentry using them to lure victims into traps. Nix is basically just another name for mermaid, siren, etc. Maybe the blessing as you stated, and the Trickery could be some form of compulsion (an opposed roll to force the target to spend it's next turn doing nothing but moving closer to the Nix?). Is that too powerful?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}